WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:09.100
- It's my pleasure today
to welcome you to this

00:00:10.687 --> 00:00:13.113
webinar from YPSA,

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:18.136
the Yale Program for the
Study of Anti-Semitism.

00:00:18.136 --> 00:00:20.070
My name is Jeff Alexander
and I'm professor

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:24.300
of sociology here at Yale
and a board member of YPSA.

00:00:25.742 --> 00:00:29.554
It's my honor and privilege
as well as a real personal

00:00:29.554 --> 00:00:33.120
pleasure to welcome my friend
and colleague Chad Goldberg,

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:34.443
to speak today.

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:39.750
Chad is the Martindale-Bascom
Professor of Sociology

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.268
at the University of Wisconsin at Madison,

00:00:43.268 --> 00:00:46.410
and the author of many articles

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:51.410
and important books of
original research and theory.

00:00:51.515 --> 00:00:54.510
But before telling you
about some of these,

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:56.910
I wanna tell you how Chad describes

00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:00.573
his research areas on
Wisconsin Sociology website.

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:06.450
He describes them as quote,
modern Jewish thought,

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:09.660
especially social and political thought,

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:13.080
the civil incorporation of
Jews as an ethno-religious

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:17.520
minority in relation to modern
state and nation building

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:20.223
and the sociology of anti-Semitism.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.660
I'm reading you this
because I can assure you

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:28.350
that it's most unusual, as far as I know,

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:31.980
Chad is the only sociologist
at a leading American

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:36.420
department to describe
his research specialties

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:38.760
as devoted entirely to what was once

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:40.803
called the Jewish question.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:46.470
In fact, Chad's first book was not

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:48.423
about Jews but about workers.

00:01:49.918 --> 00:01:52.890
It was entitled "Citizens
and Paupers: Relief, Rights,

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:56.440
and Race, from the Freedmen's
Bureau to Workfare",

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:58.865
and it won some important awards.

00:01:58.865 --> 00:02:01.590
It was in the years after that publication

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:03.450
that Chad began attending

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:07.719
to matters concerning Jewish
exclusion and incorporation.

00:02:07.719 --> 00:02:11.400
One line of which culminated
in his singular book,

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:14.373
modernity and the Jews in Western thought,

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:18.750
it was a finalist for the
National Jewish Book Award

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:21.450
and the Jordan Schnitzer Book Prize

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:23.560
and the winner of several prizes

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:26.010
from sociological societies.

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:30.720
Chad has been a fellow at
some of the world's most

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:33.120
distinguished institutes
for advanced studies,

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:35.550
including the Princeton Institute,

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:37.680
the Hanse-Wissenschaftskolleg in Berlin,

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:39.963
and the Max Weber Kolleg in Erfurt.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:44.820
He's also been the George
L. Mosse visiting professor

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:47.613
at the Hebrew University in Jerusalem.

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:52.590
Today I welcome Chad to speak at Yale.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:53.730
This talk, as you know,

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:56.520
is entitled From Multiculturalism

00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:01.520
to Antisemitism Revisiting the
Jewish Question in America.

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:02.903
Chad?

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:05.970
- Jeff, thank you so much.

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:10.020
I wanna thank you and
I wanna thank Maurice

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:12.780
for the opportunity to take
part in this webinar today.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:13.613
Jeff, I wanna thank you for

00:03:13.613 --> 00:03:15.600
that very kind introduction

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:17.910
and I wanna thank all of the attendees

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:20.250
who are here to participate as well.

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:23.370
It's a personal and professional pleasure

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:26.010
to be here with all of you today.

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:28.380
I'm gonna go ahead and see
if I can share my screen

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:31.923
with you and let me go
ahead and get started.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:39.980
My point of departure today
is Jeff's work actually,

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:44.220
which has had a strong influence on me

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:47.913
and specifically his 2006
book, the Civil Sphere.

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:54.090
Those of you who have read
this book know that nearly 90

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:59.090
pages of its 550 pages are
devoted to the Jewish question.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:00.210
As Jeff shows,

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:04.890
the Jewish question arose
in both Europe and America,

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:05.850
but in these settings,

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:08.220
the instabilities of Jewish incorporation

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:10.833
were resolved in markedly different ways.

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:15.460
I can't do justice in
my presentation today

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:19.620
to Jeff's lengthy comparison

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:22.020
of the Jewish question
in Europe and America,

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:23.820
but sufficed to say that his discussion

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:27.450
of the Jewish question in
Europe concludes with the Shoah,

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:29.730
while the corresponding
discussion of the Jewish question

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:32.990
in America ends with the
emergence in the 1960s

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:35.883
of a multicultural mode
of Jewish incorporation.

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:39.860
The startling resurgence of antisemitism

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:42.360
in the United States and the
last several years raises

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:44.490
a host of questions about the rich

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:46.710
and insightful discussion
of the Jewish question

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:49.050
that we find in the civil sphere.

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:51.600
If American Jews have been
the beneficiaries of a

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:55.500
multicultural mode of
incorporation since the 1960s,

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:58.800
how do we account for the
resurgence of antisemitism?

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:01.350
Does it mean that Jeffrey
Alexander's assessment

00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:06.030
of the Jewish question in
America was overly sanguine?

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:07.830
Alternatively, if the assessment

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:10.560
was correct for roughly half a century

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.830
from the 1960s until the 2010s,

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:16.950
does the resurgence of
antisemitism indicate another shift

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:19.890
in civil discourse that is
bringing the multicultural

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:22.890
incorporation of American Jews to an end,

00:05:22.890 --> 00:05:25.920
or is this an alarmist
overreaction to what we should

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:29.640
instead regard as a
futile rear guard backlash

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:31.380
and a temporary aberration

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:34.263
from the multicultural
incorporation of American Jewry?

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:38.040
While the contemporary
resurgence of antisemitism

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:40.680
may seem to challenge Jeff's conclusions,

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:44.160
I argue instead that his
theorization of the multicultural

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:47.280
incorporation of American
Jews helps to explain

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:50.370
the resurgence of
antisemitism in two ways,

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:52.590
by highlighting the inherent instability

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:55.230
of the multicultural
mode of incorporation,

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:58.740
and by identifying new
problems of boundary definition

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:01.893
and identity that
multiculturalism generates.

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:06.450
If contemporary antisemitism
is a backlash against

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:10.380
multiculturalist trends
that began in the 1960s,

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:13.710
then it is a backlash that
arises from the very problems

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:16.023
then multiculturalism itself produces.

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:19.560
I will develop this thesis in four parts.

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:21.000
First, I'll briefly review

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:23.460
the three modes of civil incorporation

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:25.770
that Jeff has identified
and the distinctive relation

00:06:25.770 --> 00:06:29.610
of Jews to civil society that
each of those modes entails.

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:31.500
Second, I will present evidence

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:32.990
for a resurgence of antisemitism

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:35.550
in the United States in
the past several years.

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:37.200
Third, I will trace the resurgence

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:40.680
of antisemitism in part to features

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:43.290
of the multicultural mode of incorporation

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:45.630
that Jeffrey Alexander has identified.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:48.060
Fourth, I will provide additional support

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:50.640
for this interpretation if time permits

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:52.860
by means of a historical comparison

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:54.320
to cultural attitudes toward Jews

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:57.450
in the Calvinist or
Protestant reform tradition,

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:59.730
particularly among the Puritans,

00:06:59.730 --> 00:07:04.260
and to be sure the Puritans
were not multiculturalists,

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:05.880
but they did identify themselves

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:08.070
with Jews to a remarkable degree,

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:10.890
and this identification
created similar problems

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:13.170
of boundary definition and identity,

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:16.533
which makes it, I think,
an instructive comparison.

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:22.380
So Jeffrey Alexander
examined the Jewish question

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:24.510
in relation to three ideal typical modes

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:27.630
by which excluded outgroups
have achieved incorporation

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:29.700
into the civil sphere.

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:30.690
The first of these modes

00:07:30.690 --> 00:07:33.810
of incorporation historically
was assimilation,

00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:36.420
which entails the separation
of the person who belongs

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:39.180
to an outgroup from the
stigmatized qualities

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:42.330
that distinguish the
outgroup from the core group.

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:44.760
That separation was typically accomplished

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:48.360
by means of a division between
private and public life.

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:51.790
Members of primordially
stigmatized groups could

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:54.810
participate in the discourse
and institutions of civil

00:07:54.810 --> 00:07:58.380
society insofar as they
completely shed these identities

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:00.063
upon entering the public domain.

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:03.099
Assimilation is inclusionary,

00:08:03.099 --> 00:08:05.220
in so far as it permits
the members of outgroups

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:07.380
to be evaluated positively

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:10.740
and thus affords them opportunities
for civic participation,

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:11.820
but it fails to challenge

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:14.823
the negative evaluation
of outgroup qualities.

00:08:15.990 --> 00:08:18.180
Furthermore, as Jeffrey Alexander wrote,

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:21.120
because of its delicate and tense balance

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:23.490
between negatively evaluated qualities

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:25.830
and positively evaluated persons,

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:29.490
assimilation is a highly
unstable mode of incorporation.

00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:32.040
The instabilities of the
assimilative mode of incorporation

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:35.010
allow it to be pushed
backward toward exclusion

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:38.793
or forward toward alternative
modes of civil incorporation.

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:42.870
The hyphenated mode of
incorporation began to emerge

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:45.600
in the United States at the
end of the 19th century,

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:47.280
turning immigrants and their descendants

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:51.180
into Polish Americans, Italian
Americans, and so forth.

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:52.710
Hyphenation is more open to,

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:55.830
and it accords more positive
recognition to foreign

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:57.897
or outsider particularities than does

00:08:57.897 --> 00:09:00.300
the assimilative mode of incorporation.

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:01.860
Nevertheless, it remains fraught

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:04.860
with challenges for Jews
and other outgroups.

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:06.990
While ethnic particularities
remain evident

00:09:06.990 --> 00:09:09.480
and pronounced, and this
mode of incorporation,

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:11.130
the qualities of excluded groups

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:13.350
are treated as complementary,

00:09:13.350 --> 00:09:15.650
but still inferior to
those of the core group.

00:09:16.830 --> 00:09:18.810
Alexander concluded
that the hyphenated mode

00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:21.150
of incorporation like
the assimilative mode,

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:22.860
provides a highly unstable basis

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:25.140
for the expansion of civil solidarity,

00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:27.300
and therefore is liable
to be pushed backward

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:30.330
to assimilation and even to exclusion

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:33.603
or else forward to the
multicultural mode of incorporation.

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:37.830
The multicultural mode of
incorporation goes further

00:09:37.830 --> 00:09:39.660
and differs markedly from the assimilative

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:41.820
and hyphenated modes of incorporation

00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:44.070
because it entails the positive evaluation

00:09:44.070 --> 00:09:47.940
of outgroup qualities such as
peripheral national origins,

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:50.943
minority racial status,
or marginalized religion.

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:54.270
These primordial qualities
previously thought

00:09:54.270 --> 00:09:57.480
to disqualify their bearers
from civil inclusion

00:09:57.480 --> 00:10:00.450
become reinterpreted as
representing variations

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:02.703
on the sacred qualities of civility.

00:10:03.810 --> 00:10:06.270
Following the dilemmas and
failures of the assimilative

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:07.980
and hyphenated modes of incorporation

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:09.630
earlier in the 20th century,

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:12.510
Alexander argued the
instabilities of Jewish American

00:10:12.510 --> 00:10:14.010
incorporation were pushed

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:16.743
in a multicultural direction
from the 1960s onward.

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:18.413
Simply put,

00:10:18.413 --> 00:10:20.610
Christian Americans began
to find Jewish qualities

00:10:20.610 --> 00:10:22.143
attractive in themselves.

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:24.390
Alexander's evidence for this claim

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:27.150
was mainly drawn from
American popular culture,

00:10:27.150 --> 00:10:29.910
including a close reading
of the self representations

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:31.680
of Jewish cultural producers

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:32.970
like the author Philip Roth and

00:10:32.970 --> 00:10:34.950
the actor and director Woody Allen,

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:37.503
as well as demographic
trends like intermarriage.

00:10:38.430 --> 00:10:39.840
According to this interpretation,

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:42.900
Christian Americans in
the post-war era came

00:10:42.900 --> 00:10:44.400
to view the identity

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:47.250
of the previously
marginalized Jewish outgroup,

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:48.930
both as quote legitimately

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:51.150
and importantly different from their own.

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:54.930
And at the same time, as
fundamentally the same.

00:10:54.930 --> 00:10:56.310
Unquote.

00:10:56.310 --> 00:10:58.290
Multiculturalism, Alexander concluded,

00:10:58.290 --> 00:11:02.310
requires and helps to
produce thicker and deeper

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:04.683
forms of mutual identification.

00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:09.930
If American Jews begin to experience

00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:13.140
a multicultural mode of
incorporation in the 1960s,

00:11:13.140 --> 00:11:15.723
the country's erstwhile love affair

00:11:15.723 --> 00:11:16.556
with Jewish qualities seems

00:11:16.556 --> 00:11:17.520
to have taken a disturbing turn

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:20.130
for the worst in recent years.

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:21.930
The Anti-Defamation
Defamation League established

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:24.360
in 1913 to fight anti-Semitism

00:11:24.360 --> 00:11:26.850
and other forms of
bigotry and discrimination

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:28.440
monitors anti-Semitic incidents

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:30.660
in the United States, including assaults,

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:32.463
vandalism, and harassment.

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:36.120
ADL reports indicate a steady decrease

00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:39.943
in anti-Semitism from 2011 to 2013.

00:11:39.943 --> 00:11:40.950
However,

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:42.780
the ADL reported a sharp rise

00:11:42.780 --> 00:11:45.720
in antisemitic incidents in 2014.

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:49.020
This 21% increase from the
previous year was the first time

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:52.230
in nearly a decade of declines
where the overall number of

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:54.513
incidents substantially rose.

00:11:55.770 --> 00:11:59.160
Anti-Semitic incidents
continued to increase in 2015

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:02.220
and then surged more
than one third in 2016,

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:03.720
particularly after November,

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:05.610
2016 when Donald Trump was

00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:08.370
elected president of the United States,

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:11.220
the surge continued into
the first quarter of 2017,

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:15.720
jumping 86% during the first
three months of the new year.

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:17.280
The number of antisemitic incidents

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:21.600
in 2017 ultimately rose to 1,986,

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:24.720
a 57% rise from the previous year,

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:27.720
and the largest single
year increase on record,

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:29.760
and the second highest number reported

00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:33.513
since the ADL started
tracking this data in 1979.

00:12:34.410 --> 00:12:36.738
The number of anti-Semitic incidents

00:12:36.738 --> 00:12:40.230
in the US fell slightly in 2018
before rising again in 2019.

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:42.510
Another record breaking year.

00:12:42.510 --> 00:12:43.620
Rising anti-Semitism

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:46.470
was exemplified by the
2017 Unite the Right rally

00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:48.060
in Charlottesville, Virginia,

00:12:48.060 --> 00:12:51.180
where neo-Nazis chanted
Jews will not replace us,

00:12:51.180 --> 00:12:52.430
and the murderous assault

00:12:53.448 --> 00:12:56.760
on the Pittsburgh Tree of
Life Synagogue in 2018,

00:12:56.760 --> 00:12:59.160
which the ADL described
as the deadliest attack

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:02.640
on the Jewish community in the
history of the United States.

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:05.790
The record number of anti-Semitic
incidents in 2019 included

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:09.270
deadly stabbings or shootings
of Jews at a rabbi's home

00:13:09.270 --> 00:13:12.630
in Monte, New York, a kosher
grocery store, and Jersey City,

00:13:12.630 --> 00:13:16.170
New Jersey, and a synagogue
in Poway, California.

00:13:16.170 --> 00:13:19.317
Anti-Semitic incidents
declined slightly in 2020

00:13:19.317 --> 00:13:20.150
and then reached an all time high

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:24.033
in 2021 that exceeded
even the 2019 levels.

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:27.510
And the other main
organization besides the ADL

00:13:27.510 --> 00:13:29.210
that monitors anti-Semitic incidents

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:30.120
in the United States

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:33.060
is the Federal Bureau of Investigation.

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:36.506
The FBI tracks hate crimes defined

00:13:36.506 --> 00:13:37.380
as an action of physical violence

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:39.660
or vandalism whose motive is a prejudice

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:42.390
against a specific group
and reports violence

00:13:42.390 --> 00:13:43.830
against Jews under the category

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:45.693
of prejudice based on religion,

00:13:46.770 --> 00:13:49.740
the pattern of anti-Jewish
hate crimes over time,

00:13:49.740 --> 00:13:53.490
though lower in numbers
is roughly consistent

00:13:53.490 --> 00:13:56.850
with the pattern in ADL data
on anti-Semitic incidents.

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:59.040
What we see here in this
graph is that the number

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:00.900
of anti-Jewish hate crime incidents

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:04.530
decreased steadily from 2011 through 2014.

00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:07.860
The trend that the ADL welcomed, however,

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:09.570
anti-Jewish hate crime incidents started

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:13.230
to increase in 2015 rose again in 2016,

00:14:13.230 --> 00:14:17.040
and spiked about 37% in 2017.

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:18.570
After following in 2018,

00:14:18.570 --> 00:14:23.220
anti-Jewish hate crime
incidents jumped by 14% in 2019

00:14:23.220 --> 00:14:26.580
when they comprised 13% of
all hate crime incidents,

00:14:26.580 --> 00:14:29.250
despite Jews constituting less than 2%

00:14:29.250 --> 00:14:32.790
of the US population
and fell again in 2020,

00:14:32.790 --> 00:14:34.170
though they remained higher than levels

00:14:34.170 --> 00:14:35.770
in the first half of the decade.

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:39.349
While data on hate crime incidents in 2021

00:14:39.349 --> 00:14:41.670
and 2022 were not available

00:14:41.670 --> 00:14:44.220
at the time this paper was prepared,

00:14:44.220 --> 00:14:47.310
anti-Jewish hate crimes continued
to seize public attention

00:14:47.310 --> 00:14:49.080
with the armed taking of hostages

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:53.070
at a synagogue in Colleyville,
Texas in January, 2022,

00:14:53.070 --> 00:14:55.680
and the arrest just last
week of a man threatening

00:14:55.680 --> 00:14:58.773
to kill Jewish government
officials in Michigan.

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:03.450
The rise in anti-Semitic
incidents and hate crimes

00:15:03.450 --> 00:15:05.130
is associated with a shift

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:07.770
in cultural attitudes toward
Jews in the United States.

00:15:07.770 --> 00:15:09.900
That's what I will argue at any rate,

00:15:09.900 --> 00:15:12.450
and I think there are
worrying signs of such a shift

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:15.000
on both the political left
and the political right.

00:15:17.280 --> 00:15:18.120
On the one hand,

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:21.060
the anti-Semitic motifs
of Jewish foreignness

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:25.050
or alienness exclusive
particularism, power,

00:15:25.050 --> 00:15:28.500
and wickedness parallel or correspond

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:30.570
to anti-Zionist motifs that have appeared

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:33.821
in the discourse of some
self style progressives.

00:15:33.821 --> 00:15:36.960
For example, US Representative Ilhan Omar

00:15:36.960 --> 00:15:39.547
has at various times claimed that,

00:15:39.547 --> 00:15:42.930
"Israel has hypnotized the
world while doing evil.

00:15:42.930 --> 00:15:44.480
That congressional support for Israel

00:15:44.480 --> 00:15:46.380
is quote all about the Benjamins."

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:48.390
That's to say all about money.

00:15:48.390 --> 00:15:50.707
And that American supporters of Israel,

00:15:50.707 --> 00:15:54.087
"Push for allegiance
to a foreign country."

00:15:54.087 --> 00:15:57.090
Although Omar is widely
regarded as one of the most

00:15:57.090 --> 00:15:59.460
progressive members of the US Congress,

00:15:59.460 --> 00:16:01.590
these remarks earned her the praise

00:16:01.590 --> 00:16:05.130
of former Ku Klux Klan
Grand Wizard David Duke.

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:07.350
The reason for this is
not hard to discern.

00:16:07.350 --> 00:16:08.750
Omar's rhetoric corresponds

00:16:08.750 --> 00:16:11.543
to at least two antisemitic motifs,

00:16:11.543 --> 00:16:14.370
one, that money makes Jews powerful,

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:16.080
and the other the Jews are more loyal

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:18.180
to their own interests than the country

00:16:18.180 --> 00:16:19.480
in which they're citizens.

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:23.220
Today, a segment of the American left

00:16:23.220 --> 00:16:25.140
uses the counter Democratic code

00:16:25.140 --> 00:16:27.300
and the discourse of civil society

00:16:27.300 --> 00:16:31.290
to taint American Jews who
do not embrace anti-Zionism,

00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:32.550
which is according to surveys,

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:35.043
most American Jews as bad Americans.

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:38.760
The shift in cultural attitudes
was strikingly displayed

00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:40.620
by the surge of antisemitism

00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:43.320
during the 2014 Israel Gaza conflict,

00:16:43.320 --> 00:16:46.620
which went beyond mere
criticism of Israel or Zionism

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:48.930
to include assaults on Jewish individuals

00:16:48.930 --> 00:16:51.153
and vandalism of Jewish institutions.

00:16:53.460 --> 00:16:54.293
On the other hand,

00:16:54.293 --> 00:16:56.340
under Donald Trump's
presidency from January,

00:16:56.340 --> 00:16:59.220
2017 to January, 2021,

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:02.370
the term globalist spread
from far right anti-Semitic

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:06.660
websites into mainstream
civil and political discourse.

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:09.240
The use of the term as an
anti-Jewish dog whistle received

00:17:09.240 --> 00:17:12.270
widespread attention in
2018 in connection with the

00:17:12.270 --> 00:17:15.900
resignation of Trump's chief
economic advisor, Gary Cohen,

00:17:15.900 --> 00:17:17.340
and the attempted bombing

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:20.103
of the philanthropist George
Soros' home in New York.

00:17:21.120 --> 00:17:24.570
As Aryeh Tuchman from the
Anti-Defamation League noted,

00:17:24.570 --> 00:17:26.610
the application of the
term to Jews carries

00:17:26.610 --> 00:17:28.680
a host of associations that cannot

00:17:28.680 --> 00:17:31.650
be extricated from the
history of anti-Semitism.

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:35.220
Tuchman linked the term to
long-running conspiracy theories

00:17:35.220 --> 00:17:38.250
about Jewish populations not
being loyal to the countries

00:17:38.250 --> 00:17:40.140
they live in and cooperating

00:17:40.140 --> 00:17:42.393
through secret international alliances.

00:17:43.590 --> 00:17:46.350
The anti-global representation
of Jews is in some ways

00:17:46.350 --> 00:17:49.500
antithetical to the
anti-Zionist representation.

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:52.680
Are Jews cosmopolitans or
nationalists we might ask.

00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:54.810
Nevertheless, the two discourses converge

00:17:54.810 --> 00:17:57.360
in constructing Jews as disloyal

00:17:57.360 --> 00:18:00.630
to the United States, secretive, powerful,

00:18:00.630 --> 00:18:02.463
and above all, anti-civil.

00:18:04.860 --> 00:18:07.530
The multicultural
incorporation of American Jews

00:18:07.530 --> 00:18:09.750
that began in the 1960s makes

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:12.000
the recent resurgence of antisemitism

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:14.733
appear surprising and perplexing.

00:18:15.960 --> 00:18:19.050
While claims of multicultural
incorporation seem hard

00:18:19.050 --> 00:18:22.590
to square with evidence
of rising antisemitism,

00:18:22.590 --> 00:18:24.570
I will argue that Alexander's theorization

00:18:24.570 --> 00:18:26.670
of multiculturalism reveals

00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:28.350
some of the processes that underlie

00:18:28.350 --> 00:18:30.510
this partial reversal.

00:18:30.510 --> 00:18:32.070
Since, as Alexander makes clear,

00:18:32.070 --> 00:18:35.220
the multicultural mode of
incorporation does not represent

00:18:35.220 --> 00:18:37.680
the end of an inevitable developmental

00:18:37.680 --> 00:18:39.420
or evolutionary logic,

00:18:39.420 --> 00:18:41.970
there's no reason to expect
it to remain permanent.

00:18:42.840 --> 00:18:44.010
As Alexander conceives it.

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:47.310
Multiculturalism involves
the paradoxical perception

00:18:47.310 --> 00:18:50.670
of difference as a
variation on shared humanity

00:18:50.670 --> 00:18:52.470
or the perception of outgroups

00:18:52.470 --> 00:18:54.180
as legitimately and importantly

00:18:54.180 --> 00:18:55.950
different from the core group,

00:18:55.950 --> 00:18:58.443
yet fundamentally in some sense, the same.

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:02.490
This paradox he suggests
generates problems of boundary

00:19:02.490 --> 00:19:05.910
definition and identity that
make the multicultural mode of

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:08.823
incorporation unstable in its own way.

00:19:11.610 --> 00:19:13.980
What Alexander means by this becomes clear

00:19:13.980 --> 00:19:16.500
in his discussion of the
paradoxical consequences

00:19:16.500 --> 00:19:20.370
of multicultural incorporation
for American Jews.

00:19:20.370 --> 00:19:21.990
Christian America's multicultural

00:19:21.990 --> 00:19:24.090
embrace of Jewish qualities allowed,

00:19:24.090 --> 00:19:27.270
he wrote "Confident assertions
of Jewish difference,

00:19:27.270 --> 00:19:30.240
including a return to
traditional religious practices

00:19:30.240 --> 00:19:32.100
and non-orthodox synagogues,

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:33.870
the growth of Jewish day schools

00:19:33.870 --> 00:19:35.880
and the creation of
Jewish studies departments

00:19:35.880 --> 00:19:38.247
and programs at American universities."

00:19:39.210 --> 00:19:41.810
Yet Jewish assertions of
difference were accompanied

00:19:42.688 --> 00:19:44.640
by Jewish anxiety about
the continuing viability

00:19:44.640 --> 00:19:46.830
of Judaism in America.

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:49.800
The seemingly unwarranted
anxiety was a response

00:19:49.800 --> 00:19:51.630
to the problems of boundary definition

00:19:51.630 --> 00:19:53.580
and identity that the multicultural

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:55.350
mode of incorporation generates.

00:19:55.350 --> 00:19:57.750
And here I'm quoting Jeffrey Alexander.

00:19:57.750 --> 00:20:00.720
If difference can be
recognized only when there

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:03.540
is increasing solidarity
between core and outgroup,

00:20:03.540 --> 00:20:05.580
it should not be surprising that even

00:20:05.580 --> 00:20:07.920
as they begin to cultivate
their differences,

00:20:07.920 --> 00:20:09.930
Jewish Americans would come to feel

00:20:09.930 --> 00:20:12.330
more like non-Jewish
Americans and the latter,

00:20:12.330 --> 00:20:13.163
more like them.

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:15.390
In Alexander's account,

00:20:15.390 --> 00:20:18.240
it's precisely this mutual
identification that creates

00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:21.783
anxiety about the loss of a
distinctive Jewish identity.

00:20:24.390 --> 00:20:27.600
Rising antisemitism in the
United States may reflect

00:20:27.600 --> 00:20:29.490
the problems of boundary definition

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:31.140
and identity that Alexander

00:20:31.140 --> 00:20:33.210
associated with multiculturalism,

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:35.360
but in a different way
than he anticipated.

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:39.360
If mutual identification
encourages Jewish anxiety

00:20:39.360 --> 00:20:43.110
about the continuing viability
of Judaism in America,

00:20:43.110 --> 00:20:46.290
then it is likely to foster
an analogous reaction

00:20:46.290 --> 00:20:48.723
among Americans with a Christian heritage.

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:50.393
In other words,

00:20:50.393 --> 00:20:53.640
to the extent that core
group and outgroup identities

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:56.070
are viewed as fundamentally the same,

00:20:56.070 --> 00:20:59.940
the non-Jewish core group
will also experience anxiety

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:01.740
about the continuing viability

00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:03.850
of its own identity and perhaps

00:21:04.870 --> 00:21:06.990
even the national identity
with which the core group

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:09.753
has been historically closely associated.

00:21:10.770 --> 00:21:13.380
One way this anxiety finds expression

00:21:13.380 --> 00:21:15.210
is in a renewed antisemitism,

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:18.450
and especially antisemitic
efforts to reestablish

00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:19.860
hierarchical boundaries

00:21:19.860 --> 00:21:22.533
that multiculturalism
threatens to dissolve.

00:21:24.690 --> 00:21:25.920
If the multicultural mode

00:21:25.920 --> 00:21:28.050
of incorporation generates problems

00:21:28.050 --> 00:21:30.690
of boundary definition and
identity for the core group,

00:21:30.690 --> 00:21:32.640
as well as for American Jews,

00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:34.500
there's no reason to
think that these problems

00:21:34.500 --> 00:21:36.330
will be limited to core group members

00:21:36.330 --> 00:21:40.140
who are committed to one or
another political ideology.

00:21:40.140 --> 00:21:41.430
The problems may, however,

00:21:41.430 --> 00:21:43.080
appear in somewhat different guises

00:21:43.080 --> 00:21:45.243
as a result of these
political commitments.

00:21:46.920 --> 00:21:48.090
On the one hand,

00:21:48.090 --> 00:21:49.440
breaking with the historical

00:21:49.440 --> 00:21:52.110
self consecration of
the American core group,

00:21:52.110 --> 00:21:55.440
some core group members aligned
with the progressive left

00:21:55.440 --> 00:21:57.360
are now inclined to view the core group

00:21:57.360 --> 00:21:59.820
as a deeply anti-civil oppressor

00:21:59.820 --> 00:22:02.220
of minorities and outgroups.

00:22:02.220 --> 00:22:04.710
This trans valuation of the core group

00:22:04.710 --> 00:22:06.330
by some of its own members,

00:22:06.330 --> 00:22:09.180
has adverse consequences
for the Jewish outgroup

00:22:09.180 --> 00:22:12.930
when Jews are perceived to
be fundamentally the same.

00:22:12.930 --> 00:22:16.140
Instead of viewing American
Jews as a marginalized outgroup

00:22:16.140 --> 00:22:17.730
that deserves their solidarity

00:22:17.730 --> 00:22:21.000
or allyship in contemporary
political parlance,

00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:24.000
these core group members find
it hard to distinguish Jews

00:22:24.000 --> 00:22:25.980
from other quote unquote powerful

00:22:25.980 --> 00:22:27.753
and privileged core group members.

00:22:28.950 --> 00:22:30.450
These core group members continue

00:22:30.450 --> 00:22:32.730
to see Israel as a little America,

00:22:32.730 --> 00:22:34.920
but their trans valuation
of the American core group

00:22:34.920 --> 00:22:38.190
now makes this identification polluting.

00:22:38.190 --> 00:22:39.690
Rather than interpreting Jewishness

00:22:39.690 --> 00:22:42.750
as a variation on the sacred
qualities of civility,

00:22:42.750 --> 00:22:45.510
these core group members
may instead come to see it

00:22:45.510 --> 00:22:49.530
as a variation on the profane
qualities of incivility.

00:22:49.530 --> 00:22:51.156
From there,

00:22:51.156 --> 00:22:52.290
I would say it's a small step to transfer

00:22:52.290 --> 00:22:55.740
their guilt to the Jews, their
tolerance, normalization,

00:22:55.740 --> 00:22:57.840
or in rare instances expression.

00:22:57.840 --> 00:22:59.910
Outright expressions of antisemitism,

00:22:59.910 --> 00:23:02.853
I would say is the bad
conscience of the core group.

00:23:05.490 --> 00:23:06.323
On the other hand,

00:23:06.323 --> 00:23:08.790
core group members on the
far right try to maintain

00:23:08.790 --> 00:23:11.970
restrictive primordial
definitions of civility

00:23:11.970 --> 00:23:15.153
or even to make those
definitions more narrower.

00:23:16.140 --> 00:23:19.440
Some of these core
group members blame Jews

00:23:19.440 --> 00:23:22.110
for multiculturalism, for immigration,

00:23:22.110 --> 00:23:23.880
and other developments that they think

00:23:23.880 --> 00:23:25.563
threaten the American core group.

00:23:26.520 --> 00:23:28.380
Nevertheless, they identify Jew,

00:23:28.380 --> 00:23:31.590
they identify with Jews
in surprising ways,

00:23:31.590 --> 00:23:34.830
attributing to them, and
ethnocentric culture,

00:23:34.830 --> 00:23:37.020
which they believe advantages Jews

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:39.540
and is at odds with the multiculturalism

00:23:39.540 --> 00:23:41.823
that they believe Jews foist on others.

00:23:42.840 --> 00:23:46.563
Their hatred of Jews is in
this way conjoined with envy.

00:23:47.700 --> 00:23:51.270
This perspective shapes
attitudes toward Israel as well.

00:23:51.270 --> 00:23:52.950
For instance, in 2017,

00:23:52.950 --> 00:23:56.100
the white nationalist Richard
Spencer described himself

00:23:56.100 --> 00:24:00.090
to an Israeli journalist
as a "White Zionist",

00:24:00.090 --> 00:24:01.957
and insisted to the journalist that,

00:24:01.957 --> 00:24:05.310
"You should respect someone
like me who understands

00:24:05.310 --> 00:24:08.370
your identity and the
experience of the Jewish people,

00:24:08.370 --> 00:24:10.857
and has analog feelings about whites."

00:24:12.660 --> 00:24:15.540
Notwithstanding Spencer's spurious analogy

00:24:15.540 --> 00:24:17.940
and distorted understanding of Zionism,

00:24:17.940 --> 00:24:21.450
these comments reveal the
ambivalence of core group members

00:24:21.450 --> 00:24:24.240
on the far right who see Jews as a threat

00:24:24.240 --> 00:24:28.140
and simultaneously project
their own wishes onto them.

00:24:28.140 --> 00:24:30.060
The portrait of the Jews that they offer

00:24:30.060 --> 00:24:33.483
to the world is in fact
their own self-portrait.

00:24:35.280 --> 00:24:38.220
This theoretical argument
about the American core group

00:24:38.220 --> 00:24:41.400
and its relation to
Jews needs qualification

00:24:41.400 --> 00:24:42.780
in a few key respects,

00:24:42.780 --> 00:24:44.480
and so I wanna mention those here.

00:24:46.050 --> 00:24:48.360
First, I don't want to suggest,

00:24:48.360 --> 00:24:50.280
and I don't mean to suggest

00:24:50.280 --> 00:24:55.280
that the entire American core
group has become anti-Semitic.

00:24:56.010 --> 00:24:58.740
Rather, problems of boundary definition

00:24:58.740 --> 00:25:02.040
and identity facilitate
tolerance, normalization,

00:25:02.040 --> 00:25:04.590
or even outright
expressions of anti-Semitism

00:25:04.590 --> 00:25:07.470
among core group members
making such expressions

00:25:07.470 --> 00:25:09.993
more likely within the group.

00:25:13.260 --> 00:25:16.860
Second, Christianity is only
one of the primordial qualities

00:25:16.860 --> 00:25:19.170
available for defining
the American core group

00:25:19.170 --> 00:25:21.840
and judging civil competence.

00:25:21.840 --> 00:25:24.330
Nevertheless, following Alexander,

00:25:24.330 --> 00:25:27.570
the Christian qualities
analytically accentuated here

00:25:27.570 --> 00:25:29.340
because of its particular significance

00:25:29.340 --> 00:25:30.840
vis-a-vis the Jewish outgroup.

00:25:32.010 --> 00:25:35.520
And third, while this theoretical argument

00:25:35.520 --> 00:25:38.070
is about the core group
in its relation to Jews,

00:25:38.070 --> 00:25:40.260
it raises questions about
the growing minority

00:25:40.260 --> 00:25:43.560
of Americans who are
religiously unaffiliated,

00:25:43.560 --> 00:25:46.860
which according to survey
research now make up

00:25:46.860 --> 00:25:49.170
about 29% of all Americans,

00:25:49.170 --> 00:25:51.540
as well as the very small
minority of Americans

00:25:51.540 --> 00:25:53.430
who are religiously affiliated,

00:25:53.430 --> 00:25:54.990
but belong neither to America's

00:25:54.990 --> 00:25:57.150
historically Christian core group,

00:25:57.150 --> 00:26:00.480
nor to the Jewish outgroup
and survey data suggests

00:26:00.480 --> 00:26:04.623
that those Americans make up
about 4% of the population.

00:26:06.270 --> 00:26:09.300
Many religiously
unaffiliated Americans belong

00:26:09.300 --> 00:26:12.390
to the Christian core
group by cultural heritage.

00:26:12.390 --> 00:26:15.450
Even if they do not identify as Christian,

00:26:15.450 --> 00:26:19.230
they may have no use for
Christianity as church or credo,

00:26:19.230 --> 00:26:21.060
but its cultural influence endures

00:26:21.060 --> 00:26:23.523
in the form of secularized Christianity.

00:26:24.360 --> 00:26:27.420
They're therefore likely I
would submit to share in some

00:26:27.420 --> 00:26:31.237
form the anxieties that
the multicultural mode of

00:26:31.237 --> 00:26:33.863
incorporation generates among
other core group members.

00:26:34.920 --> 00:26:37.620
However, the anxieties of
someone like Ilhan Omar

00:26:37.620 --> 00:26:39.240
would be more complicated.

00:26:39.240 --> 00:26:41.460
Since Muslim Americans have arguably

00:26:41.460 --> 00:26:44.610
not experienced a multicultural
mode of incorporation,

00:26:44.610 --> 00:26:46.770
their identities may be
more divided in a manner

00:26:46.770 --> 00:26:50.133
characteristic of hyphenation
or even double consciousness.

00:26:50.970 --> 00:26:52.740
In addition, the relative success

00:26:52.740 --> 00:26:54.420
of the multicultural incorporation

00:26:54.420 --> 00:26:56.880
of Jewish Americans since the 1960s

00:26:56.880 --> 00:26:59.970
may lead such minorities
to resent an outgroup

00:26:59.970 --> 00:27:02.420
that they perceive to have
joined the core group.

00:27:03.510 --> 00:27:05.823
In my view, this is a mistaken perception,

00:27:06.960 --> 00:27:09.150
and it's mistaken, I
think for a few reasons.

00:27:09.150 --> 00:27:12.420
One, even in ideal typical form,

00:27:12.420 --> 00:27:15.630
multiculturalism does not
simply absorb outgroups

00:27:15.630 --> 00:27:18.000
into an expanded core group.

00:27:18.000 --> 00:27:20.460
Rather, outgroups are
paradoxically perceived

00:27:20.460 --> 00:27:22.830
as both legitimately and
importantly different

00:27:22.830 --> 00:27:25.893
from the core group, and
as fundamentally the same.

00:27:27.330 --> 00:27:30.030
Second, the multicultural
mode of incorporation

00:27:30.030 --> 00:27:34.020
takes incomplete or uneven
forms in real civil societies,

00:27:34.020 --> 00:27:36.750
in part because it
overlaps with past modes

00:27:36.750 --> 00:27:39.813
of incorporation that partly
survive into the present.

00:27:40.860 --> 00:27:42.810
And third, and this in a way,

00:27:42.810 --> 00:27:44.430
is part of the point of this paper

00:27:44.430 --> 00:27:46.890
as a whole renewed antisemitism,

00:27:46.890 --> 00:27:48.330
belies the assumption that Jews

00:27:48.330 --> 00:27:50.310
are now part of the American core group

00:27:50.310 --> 00:27:53.103
in any simple or straightforward sense.

00:27:58.323 --> 00:28:00.630
Let me turn to the last
part of my paper here,

00:28:00.630 --> 00:28:05.433
and I hope you'll indulge
me with this excursus,

00:28:06.570 --> 00:28:07.950
the multicultural mode

00:28:07.950 --> 00:28:10.680
of civil incorporation is quite new

00:28:10.680 --> 00:28:13.020
in the history of Western societies.

00:28:13.020 --> 00:28:15.720
Nevertheless, I think historical analogies

00:28:15.720 --> 00:28:17.013
can still be instructive.

00:28:17.910 --> 00:28:20.970
Despite the millennia-long
Christian pollution of Jews

00:28:20.970 --> 00:28:22.920
as incapable of participating

00:28:22.920 --> 00:28:25.290
in the civic life of Christian societies,

00:28:25.290 --> 00:28:28.260
we can find exceptional
cases in which members

00:28:28.260 --> 00:28:30.540
of a Christian core group identified

00:28:30.540 --> 00:28:33.993
in relatively thick and deep
ways with the Jewish outgroup.

00:28:35.070 --> 00:28:37.110
Such identification usually involve

00:28:37.110 --> 00:28:40.890
a positive evaluation of
not only Jewish persons,

00:28:40.890 --> 00:28:42.990
but also some Jewish qualities

00:28:42.990 --> 00:28:45.573
such as chosenness and biblical truth.

00:28:46.800 --> 00:28:47.700
And these instances,

00:28:47.700 --> 00:28:49.980
some Christians came
to see Jewish identity

00:28:49.980 --> 00:28:52.620
as importantly different
from the core groups,

00:28:52.620 --> 00:28:55.173
and at the same time as
fundamentally the same,

00:28:56.070 --> 00:28:59.760
their views anticipated
multiculturalism in this respect,

00:28:59.760 --> 00:29:02.730
even if Christian theological
assumptions prevented

00:29:02.730 --> 00:29:05.733
their views from developing
fully in this direction,

00:29:06.720 --> 00:29:09.330
cultural attitudes toward
Jews in the Calvinist

00:29:09.330 --> 00:29:11.430
or Protestant reformed tradition,

00:29:11.430 --> 00:29:13.140
particularly among the Puritans,

00:29:13.140 --> 00:29:15.003
may provide the best example.

00:29:16.230 --> 00:29:20.733
Puritanism always felt its
inner similarity to Judaism,

00:29:21.644 --> 00:29:23.779
Max Faber wrote, even if it also felt

00:29:23.779 --> 00:29:25.530
the limits of the similarity.

00:29:25.530 --> 00:29:27.930
Consequently, I will suggest Puritans

00:29:27.930 --> 00:29:30.180
experienced problems
of boundary definition

00:29:30.180 --> 00:29:34.350
and identity similar to those
generated by multiculturalism,

00:29:34.350 --> 00:29:36.630
and they manage the
resulting anxieties in ways

00:29:36.630 --> 00:29:38.910
that illuminate the
contemporary resurgence

00:29:38.910 --> 00:29:40.893
of antisemitism in the United States.

00:29:42.930 --> 00:29:45.750
The Protestant Reformation
in the 16th century gave rise

00:29:45.750 --> 00:29:47.850
to intense religious conflicts

00:29:47.850 --> 00:29:49.830
and sectarian struggles among Christians

00:29:49.830 --> 00:29:51.630
in which each faction frequently

00:29:51.630 --> 00:29:54.030
accused the others of Judaism.

00:29:54.030 --> 00:29:56.310
For example, a Bavarian Catholic preached

00:29:56.310 --> 00:29:59.610
in a 1551 sermon that the king of England,

00:29:59.610 --> 00:30:02.130
at that time, the Protestant Edward VI,

00:30:02.130 --> 00:30:05.313
his council and Kingdom
had all become Jews.

00:30:06.150 --> 00:30:08.040
The Church of England
soon turned the charge

00:30:08.040 --> 00:30:10.380
against its own internal dissenters

00:30:10.380 --> 00:30:12.902
labeling Puritans as judaizers

00:30:12.902 --> 00:30:15.000
in the late 16th century
in the association

00:30:15.000 --> 00:30:17.670
between Puritanism and
Judaism was formally

00:30:17.670 --> 00:30:21.240
in place as the 17th century got underway.

00:30:21.240 --> 00:30:22.073
But in this instance,

00:30:22.073 --> 00:30:23.760
the charge was more than a stigmatizing

00:30:23.760 --> 00:30:26.400
label used to discredit rivals.

00:30:26.400 --> 00:30:29.610
The Puritans were convinced
that they were the true Jews,

00:30:29.610 --> 00:30:31.860
the ultimate and total
heirs of the promises

00:30:31.860 --> 00:30:34.290
that God had made in the Hebrew Bible,

00:30:34.290 --> 00:30:36.830
and the strong identification
expressed itself

00:30:36.830 --> 00:30:40.080
in a variety of judaizing
practices summarized

00:30:40.080 --> 00:30:41.883
by the historian Eliana Glazer,

00:30:42.870 --> 00:30:44.820
and I'm quoting Glazer here.

00:30:44.820 --> 00:30:47.490
Puritans attempted to strip
away what they regarded

00:30:47.490 --> 00:30:51.000
as corrupt layers of Episcopal authority

00:30:51.000 --> 00:30:53.520
and popish ceremonial and reclaimed

00:30:53.520 --> 00:30:56.610
the original apostolic Christian faith.

00:30:56.610 --> 00:30:59.490
They justified their position
by invoking the Bible,

00:30:59.490 --> 00:31:01.500
and particularly the Old Testament,

00:31:01.500 --> 00:31:04.449
and they believed that
scripture should be read

00:31:04.449 --> 00:31:05.745
in the original Hebrew.

00:31:05.745 --> 00:31:08.220
Puritans advocated the use of
Hebrew in biblical translation

00:31:08.220 --> 00:31:09.870
and scriptural exegesis,

00:31:09.870 --> 00:31:12.960
and they identified with
the biblical chosen people.

00:31:12.960 --> 00:31:14.100
In addition, many puritans

00:31:14.100 --> 00:31:16.770
became scholars of
post-biblical Jewish literature

00:31:16.770 --> 00:31:19.980
such as the Talmud, and
most heterodox of all,

00:31:19.980 --> 00:31:22.530
some even began to adopt Jewish practices

00:31:22.530 --> 00:31:25.503
and customs such as the
Sabbath and Passover.

00:31:27.480 --> 00:31:30.540
Puritan identification
with Jews created problems

00:31:30.540 --> 00:31:33.420
of boundary definition
and identity analogous

00:31:33.420 --> 00:31:35.790
to those that arise in multiculturalism,

00:31:35.790 --> 00:31:38.580
which fueled anxiety about
the continuing viability

00:31:38.580 --> 00:31:40.800
of their own religious identity.

00:31:40.800 --> 00:31:43.470
The Puritans consequently
tried to reassert boundaries

00:31:43.470 --> 00:31:48.242
that have become obscured, and
this is evident, for example,

00:31:48.242 --> 00:31:50.610
in conflicts over whether
to readmit Jews into England

00:31:50.610 --> 00:31:53.610
and whether to admit them into
the Massachusetts Bay Colony.

00:31:55.110 --> 00:31:59.040
The debate in 1655 to 1656
over whether to readmit Jews

00:31:59.040 --> 00:32:01.260
into England following their expulsion

00:32:01.260 --> 00:32:03.690
in 1290 was shaped in part

00:32:03.690 --> 00:32:07.134
by Puritan Semitism and Arianism.

00:32:07.134 --> 00:32:09.750
The public practices
of Christian judaizers

00:32:09.750 --> 00:32:11.700
and the growth of interest in Hebrew

00:32:11.700 --> 00:32:12.800
had already helped to put Jews

00:32:12.800 --> 00:32:15.780
in a favorable light among
Protestant reformers,

00:32:15.780 --> 00:32:18.430
some of whom came to believe
that the return of Jews

00:32:19.733 --> 00:32:22.380
to England would hasten the
second coming of Christ.

00:32:22.380 --> 00:32:23.640
Not surprisingly then,

00:32:23.640 --> 00:32:27.060
some of the most strident
devotees of the mid 17th century

00:32:27.060 --> 00:32:30.213
Puritan Revolution favored
readmission of Jews.

00:32:31.290 --> 00:32:33.840
The historian Roger Healy
suggests that the readmission

00:32:33.840 --> 00:32:36.630
movement failed because
not enough English believed

00:32:36.630 --> 00:32:38.490
that the Jews were future Christians

00:32:38.490 --> 00:32:40.293
and harbingers of the millennium.

00:32:41.310 --> 00:32:43.020
However, opposition to the readmission

00:32:43.020 --> 00:32:45.750
of Jews also sprang from a deeper fear,

00:32:45.750 --> 00:32:47.040
namely that it would result

00:32:47.040 --> 00:32:48.960
in the utilization of Christians,

00:32:48.960 --> 00:32:51.933
and thus the loss of a
distinctive Christian identity.

00:32:53.190 --> 00:32:54.390
Among religious leaders,

00:32:55.349 --> 00:32:57.887
there were many who liked
the Puritan pamphleteer,

00:32:57.887 --> 00:32:58.720
William Prin,

00:32:58.720 --> 00:32:59.640
believed that if the Jews were readmitted,

00:32:59.640 --> 00:33:02.130
the Christians "Would sooner turn Jews

00:33:02.130 --> 00:33:03.507
than the Jews Christians."

00:33:04.950 --> 00:33:06.990
One response to this boundary crisis was

00:33:06.990 --> 00:33:09.000
to keep Jews out of England.

00:33:09.000 --> 00:33:11.190
The symbolic logic is
apparent, for example,

00:33:11.190 --> 00:33:13.646
in the writings of the 17th century

00:33:13.646 --> 00:33:15.210
political philosopher James Harrington.

00:33:15.210 --> 00:33:16.560
Although Harrington advocated

00:33:16.560 --> 00:33:18.660
a theocratic republic in England,

00:33:18.660 --> 00:33:20.310
modeled on the Hebrew commonwealth,

00:33:20.310 --> 00:33:24.090
established through Moses
fear of judaization led him

00:33:24.090 --> 00:33:26.880
to oppose the readmission of Jews.

00:33:26.880 --> 00:33:28.140
He proposed instead,

00:33:28.140 --> 00:33:30.990
the establishment of a
colony of Jews in Ireland

00:33:30.990 --> 00:33:33.510
where they could be
profitable to the republic,

00:33:33.510 --> 00:33:35.493
but safely separate from it.

00:33:36.840 --> 00:33:38.910
As the sociologist Kai Erikson points out

00:33:38.910 --> 00:33:42.060
in his classic study of
deviance in Puritan New England,

00:33:42.060 --> 00:33:43.620
communities maintain their boundaries

00:33:43.620 --> 00:33:46.530
in geographical as well as cultural space.

00:33:46.530 --> 00:33:47.857
And here I'm quoting Erikson,

00:33:47.857 --> 00:33:50.340
"Both of these dimensions of group space,

00:33:50.340 --> 00:33:52.500
the geographical and the cultural,

00:33:52.500 --> 00:33:55.410
set the community apart as a special place

00:33:55.410 --> 00:33:57.404
and provide an important

00:33:57.404 --> 00:33:59.550
point of reference for its members."

00:33:59.550 --> 00:34:02.070
And the debate over
readmission of Jews to England,

00:34:02.070 --> 00:34:04.290
maintenance of geographical
boundaries served

00:34:04.290 --> 00:34:07.443
to compensate for the obscuring
of cultural boundaries.

00:34:09.513 --> 00:34:11.250
Like the English Puritans,

00:34:11.250 --> 00:34:13.740
their counterparts in New
England similarly struggled

00:34:13.740 --> 00:34:15.330
to redefine boundaries

00:34:15.330 --> 00:34:18.840
that their philosemitism
threatened to dissolve.

00:34:18.840 --> 00:34:20.220
To be sure identification

00:34:20.220 --> 00:34:21.690
with Jews was not the only source

00:34:21.690 --> 00:34:23.910
of boundary definition
and identity problems

00:34:23.910 --> 00:34:25.050
in the new world.

00:34:25.050 --> 00:34:27.060
But Puritan identification
with Jews threatened

00:34:27.060 --> 00:34:29.030
to obscure the cultural boundaries

00:34:29.030 --> 00:34:30.200
of the Puritan community

00:34:30.200 --> 00:34:32.850
in its own way and compounded anxiety

00:34:32.850 --> 00:34:35.733
about the continuing viability
of Puritanism in America.

00:34:36.840 --> 00:34:40.590
Erikson analyzed the
Antinomian controversy of 1636,

00:34:40.590 --> 00:34:43.650
the Quaker persecutions of the late 1650s,

00:34:43.650 --> 00:34:48.030
and the witchcraft hysteria
of 1692 as different attempts

00:34:48.030 --> 00:34:50.280
by the people of the Massachusetts Bay

00:34:50.280 --> 00:34:53.711
to clarify their position
in the world as a whole,

00:34:53.711 --> 00:34:55.920
to redefine the boundaries
which set New England apart

00:34:55.920 --> 00:34:57.753
as a new experiment in living.

00:34:58.680 --> 00:35:01.410
The inhospitable and
exclusionary practices

00:35:01.410 --> 00:35:03.390
that New England Puritans adopted

00:35:03.390 --> 00:35:05.100
toward the handful of
Jews they encountered

00:35:05.100 --> 00:35:09.000
in the 17th century may be
understood in the same way,

00:35:09.000 --> 00:35:11.430
although New England
Puritans persecuted Quakers

00:35:11.430 --> 00:35:12.843
more severely than Jews,

00:35:13.807 --> 00:35:17.190
exclusion of Jews was rooted
in the same symbolic quandary.

00:35:17.190 --> 00:35:18.999
Here I'm quoting Erikson,

00:35:18.999 --> 00:35:20.610
it was exactly because the
New England Puritans shared

00:35:20.610 --> 00:35:23.070
so many features in
common with the Quakers,

00:35:23.070 --> 00:35:25.950
that they had to publicize
the few crucial differences

00:35:25.950 --> 00:35:28.350
as noisily as they could to mark

00:35:28.350 --> 00:35:30.720
off a new set of boundaries
for the New England way.

00:35:30.720 --> 00:35:32.940
They had to make a particular
effort to emphasize

00:35:32.940 --> 00:35:34.620
those points where the Puritan

00:35:34.620 --> 00:35:36.513
and Quaker streams diverged.

00:35:37.770 --> 00:35:39.540
The New England Puritans
treatment of the Jews

00:35:39.540 --> 00:35:41.607
they encountered events,

00:35:41.607 --> 00:35:43.650
an analogous effort to mark
off boundaries and keep

00:35:43.650 --> 00:35:47.373
a group with whom they shared
many features safely separate.

00:35:48.300 --> 00:35:51.360
So in some puritans were
not multiculturalists,

00:35:51.360 --> 00:35:54.210
but they did identify with
Jews to an unusual degree.

00:35:54.210 --> 00:35:56.880
And this identification
generated problems of boundary

00:35:56.880 --> 00:35:59.970
definition and identity
similar to those that arise

00:35:59.970 --> 00:36:02.640
from the multicultural
mode of incorporation.

00:36:02.640 --> 00:36:05.250
Consequently, the Puritans
experienced anxiety

00:36:05.250 --> 00:36:06.630
about the continuing viability

00:36:06.630 --> 00:36:08.550
of their religious movement and the loss

00:36:08.550 --> 00:36:10.890
of their own distinctive
religious identity.

00:36:10.890 --> 00:36:12.900
If they saw Jews as future Christians,

00:36:12.900 --> 00:36:15.930
they also worried that they
themselves might become Jews.

00:36:15.930 --> 00:36:18.093
The closer their identification with Jews,

00:36:19.028 --> 00:36:20.794
the more they found it necessary

00:36:20.794 --> 00:36:21.683
to keep Jews at arm's length.

00:36:22.720 --> 00:36:23.580
As the boundaries that set Puritanism

00:36:23.580 --> 00:36:26.100
apart threatened to become more obscure.

00:36:26.100 --> 00:36:28.920
They strove to mark off
a new set of boundaries

00:36:28.920 --> 00:36:31.320
by excluding Jews from the geographical

00:36:31.320 --> 00:36:33.723
or cultural space that
the community occupied.

00:36:34.560 --> 00:36:35.393
And this history,

00:36:35.393 --> 00:36:37.680
I would submit finds it's parallel

00:36:37.680 --> 00:36:40.470
and contemporary fears
that Jewish Zionists

00:36:40.470 --> 00:36:44.220
and globalists are
figuratively judaizing America,

00:36:44.220 --> 00:36:46.740
and in anti-Semitic
efforts to exclude Jews

00:36:46.740 --> 00:36:47.913
from the civil sphere.

00:36:49.710 --> 00:36:53.730
To conclude, while there is
persuasive evidence of a shift,

00:36:53.730 --> 00:36:56.730
beginning in the 1960s toward
a multicultural mode of

00:36:56.730 --> 00:36:59.190
incorporation for American Jews,

00:36:59.190 --> 00:37:02.430
the resurgence of
antisemitism in recent years

00:37:02.430 --> 00:37:05.610
in the form of a sharp rise
in antisemitic incidents,

00:37:05.610 --> 00:37:08.460
as well as changing patterns
of discourse and cultural

00:37:08.460 --> 00:37:09.780
representation underscores

00:37:09.780 --> 00:37:12.903
the instability of this
mode of incorporation.

00:37:13.860 --> 00:37:15.630
After a half century of multicultural

00:37:15.630 --> 00:37:17.520
incorporation of American Jews.

00:37:17.520 --> 00:37:20.970
How and why is antisemitism
now on the rise?

00:37:20.970 --> 00:37:23.880
A theory that posits the
multicultural incorporation

00:37:23.880 --> 00:37:25.140
of American Jews would seem

00:37:25.140 --> 00:37:27.060
to have difficulty explaining the

00:37:27.060 --> 00:37:29.100
revival of antisemitism.

00:37:29.100 --> 00:37:31.290
But in fact, Jeffrey Alexander's analysis

00:37:31.290 --> 00:37:34.140
of multiculturalism
provides important clues

00:37:34.140 --> 00:37:37.020
for understanding its partial reversal.

00:37:37.020 --> 00:37:40.110
His analysis acknowledged the instability

00:37:40.110 --> 00:37:42.330
of the multicultural mode of incorporation

00:37:42.330 --> 00:37:45.240
and traced it to the new
problems of boundary definition

00:37:45.240 --> 00:37:49.020
and identity that
multiculturalism generates.

00:37:49.020 --> 00:37:50.010
According to Alexander,

00:37:50.010 --> 00:37:53.940
these problems explained why
American Jews felt anxiety

00:37:53.940 --> 00:37:56.820
about the continuing viability
of Judaism in America,

00:37:56.820 --> 00:37:59.730
despite an unparalleled
embrace of Jewish qualities

00:37:59.730 --> 00:38:01.950
by the Christian core group.

00:38:01.950 --> 00:38:05.220
What I have argued here
today is that these problems

00:38:05.220 --> 00:38:07.440
of boundary definition and identity

00:38:07.440 --> 00:38:09.810
also generate corresponding anxieties

00:38:09.810 --> 00:38:11.940
among members of the Christian core group,

00:38:11.940 --> 00:38:14.610
and these anxieties are
contributing to the resurgence

00:38:14.610 --> 00:38:17.463
of antisemitism and the
United States today.

00:38:18.630 --> 00:38:19.480
Thanks very much.

00:38:20.580 --> 00:38:23.100
- Oh, thank you very much, Chad.

00:38:23.100 --> 00:38:26.700
I'm not able to get myself
on the screen at this point,

00:38:26.700 --> 00:38:28.320
but you can hear me, right?

00:38:28.320 --> 00:38:29.153
Yes.

00:38:30.414 --> 00:38:31.247
- There we go.

00:38:35.114 --> 00:38:37.050
And I will answer to them.

00:38:37.050 --> 00:38:39.903
I will ask them for you to chat.

00:38:43.110 --> 00:38:47.520
Well, one question that might be helpful

00:38:47.520 --> 00:38:48.640
to answer is

00:38:52.650 --> 00:38:55.110
by David Foreign.

00:38:55.110 --> 00:38:57.603
He asks, what is boundary definition?

00:38:59.100 --> 00:39:02.160
- Yeah, so I mean,

00:39:02.160 --> 00:39:05.970
I am drawing here on Jeff's work,

00:39:05.970 --> 00:39:09.060
but also in the work of Kai
Erikson and some others,

00:39:09.060 --> 00:39:12.180
all of whom sort of
emphasized the importance,

00:39:12.180 --> 00:39:16.811
to groups and communities
of having clear boundaries

00:39:16.811 --> 00:39:20.280
that set the identities
of those groups apart,

00:39:20.280 --> 00:39:24.440
that distinguish them
in some way and allow

00:39:24.440 --> 00:39:29.440
the members of those groups to
consecrate their identities,

00:39:31.140 --> 00:39:35.190
their ways of life, their
practices as somehow special,

00:39:35.190 --> 00:39:36.093
distinctive,

00:39:40.059 --> 00:39:41.309
and worthy of difference.

00:39:42.859 --> 00:39:45.371
So I guess what I would say then

00:39:45.371 --> 00:39:46.530
is that the boundary definition has

00:39:46.530 --> 00:39:50.310
to do with how any community,

00:39:50.310 --> 00:39:54.510
any cultural group distinguishes
itself from others,

00:39:54.510 --> 00:39:56.853
how it defines itself,

00:39:57.992 --> 00:39:59.820
and any process of self-definition
is going to involve

00:39:59.820 --> 00:40:02.520
a process of distinction
that it's going to,

00:40:02.520 --> 00:40:05.400
in some way set itself apart from others,

00:40:05.400 --> 00:40:06.240
not necessarily,

00:40:06.240 --> 00:40:08.489
I think, in an insidious way.

00:40:08.489 --> 00:40:10.380
And I don't think that
this kind of boundary work

00:40:10.380 --> 00:40:15.380
is inherently bad or
detrimental to other groups.

00:40:16.440 --> 00:40:21.003
I think it's just part of
how identity formation works.

00:40:22.030 --> 00:40:22.863
So that's what I have in mind

00:40:22.863 --> 00:40:24.963
when I talk about boundary definition.

00:40:25.824 --> 00:40:27.563
I hope that makes it a little bit clearer.

00:40:31.440 --> 00:40:34.660
- Yes, that's important
for non-sociologists

00:40:36.061 --> 00:40:37.863
to get some of the terms out there.

00:40:39.330 --> 00:40:42.990
Here's another question
for you from Rena Seltzer.

00:40:42.990 --> 00:40:47.400
She asked, how does the woke ideology,

00:40:47.400 --> 00:40:49.570
which promotes antisemitism

00:40:50.880 --> 00:40:54.153
by defining Jews as privileged oppressors,

00:40:55.500 --> 00:40:59.290
and through intersectionality
defining Zionism

00:41:00.150 --> 00:41:02.703
and Israel as colonialists,

00:41:02.703 --> 00:41:07.023
how does this woke ideology
fit into your schema?

00:41:10.688 --> 00:41:12.390
- Yeah, so I, you know,

00:41:12.390 --> 00:41:14.350
I think there's a lot of debate about

00:41:15.480 --> 00:41:19.012
this term and what it means,

00:41:19.012 --> 00:41:21.540
and people use it in different ways.

00:41:21.540 --> 00:41:22.860
Some people use it very broadly.

00:41:22.860 --> 00:41:27.363
Some people use it in sort
of more specific ways.

00:41:30.930 --> 00:41:35.400
I think I touched on this when
I talked about members of,

00:41:35.400 --> 00:41:36.840
again, not all members of the core group,

00:41:36.840 --> 00:41:39.813
but some members of the
core group who have,

00:41:42.330 --> 00:41:43.860
who have been involved,

00:41:43.860 --> 00:41:45.725
in what we could describe

00:41:45.725 --> 00:41:47.805
as a trans valuation of
the core group itself.

00:41:47.805 --> 00:41:49.080
So again, the point that I tried to make,

00:41:49.080 --> 00:41:50.940
and maybe I went through this
a little bit too quickly,

00:41:50.940 --> 00:41:52.083
and maybe it was lost,

00:41:53.052 --> 00:41:55.260
is that what to me is a
really interesting process

00:41:55.260 --> 00:41:56.520
sociologically and culturally,

00:41:56.520 --> 00:41:59.340
is that you have people that are,

00:41:59.340 --> 00:42:01.530
I think members of the core
group, not exclusively,

00:42:01.530 --> 00:42:02.940
but some of them are core group members

00:42:02.940 --> 00:42:05.880
or have that cultural heritage

00:42:05.880 --> 00:42:10.342
who have come to regard the core group

00:42:10.342 --> 00:42:13.953
that they belong to as deeply anti-civil.

00:42:14.790 --> 00:42:19.620
And so what I suggested is that this is,

00:42:19.620 --> 00:42:21.813
my argument is less about the ideology.

00:42:22.780 --> 00:42:25.650
So I think the roots of
antisemitism lie less in ideology

00:42:25.650 --> 00:42:27.330
than in these new problems

00:42:27.330 --> 00:42:31.233
of boundary definition and identity.

00:42:32.280 --> 00:42:34.140
This term that I borrowed from Jeff's work

00:42:34.140 --> 00:42:36.660
in his and civil sphere theory,

00:42:36.660 --> 00:42:41.040
which are really sort of
cultural and structural problems

00:42:41.040 --> 00:42:43.950
generated by the multicultural
mode of incorporation.

00:42:43.950 --> 00:42:47.520
So my argument is not really
about the effects of ideology.

00:42:47.520 --> 00:42:49.260
I think maybe the way that ideology,

00:42:49.260 --> 00:42:52.080
political ideologies come into play here

00:42:52.080 --> 00:42:55.050
is that they mediate and they shape

00:42:55.050 --> 00:42:58.170
how members of the core group make

00:42:58.170 --> 00:42:59.340
sense of these anxieties

00:42:59.340 --> 00:43:03.262
and how they respond to these anxieties.

00:43:03.262 --> 00:43:05.333
And so there, I think
we see some variation,

00:43:06.462 --> 00:43:11.462
but I don't think that
antisemitism is a product

00:43:15.765 --> 00:43:18.497
of one and only one political ideology.

00:43:18.497 --> 00:43:19.800
I think there's a variety of ideologies

00:43:19.800 --> 00:43:23.410
that we can find in the American
political landscape today.

00:43:23.410 --> 00:43:27.870
And I'm struck and worried by what I see

00:43:27.870 --> 00:43:29.490
as expressions of antisemitism

00:43:29.490 --> 00:43:31.340
or at least tolerance of antisemitism

00:43:32.321 --> 00:43:34.020
on different sides of the political divide

00:43:34.020 --> 00:43:35.320
in the political spectrum.

00:43:36.674 --> 00:43:40.563
So, there is a connection,

00:43:41.702 --> 00:43:43.361
but I wouldn't say,

00:43:43.361 --> 00:43:44.790
and I don't argue in this paper

00:43:45.876 --> 00:43:47.651
that a political ideology,

00:43:47.651 --> 00:43:49.883
woke or otherwise, is the
source of these problems.

00:43:51.990 --> 00:43:52.830
- Thank you.

00:43:52.830 --> 00:43:56.523
Now we have a question kind
of from the opposite side.

00:43:58.590 --> 00:43:59.943
This is anonymous.

00:44:02.140 --> 00:44:06.270
So he says, why in
anti-Semitism historically

00:44:06.270 --> 00:44:08.010
has been correlated with

00:44:08.010 --> 00:44:11.250
an income inequality and social unrest,

00:44:11.250 --> 00:44:15.360
given the extreme income
inequality in America today,

00:44:15.360 --> 00:44:17.340
do you think this plays or has played

00:44:17.340 --> 00:44:19.923
a role in the rise of anti-Semitism?

00:44:22.590 --> 00:44:23.643
- Yeah, interesting.

00:44:29.790 --> 00:44:31.852
I think so.

00:44:31.852 --> 00:44:34.983
I think the roots of antisemitism
are multiple and complex.

00:44:38.430 --> 00:44:42.030
I think that there can be a conjuncture

00:44:42.030 --> 00:44:43.683
of different factors at work,

00:44:44.790 --> 00:44:49.770
and I think the globalist language

00:44:49.770 --> 00:44:52.030
that I talked about is maybe a way in

00:44:53.298 --> 00:44:57.480
which anxiety's about
growing economic inequality

00:44:57.480 --> 00:45:01.473
get linked to antipathy
or hostility toward Jews.

00:45:05.670 --> 00:45:10.200
And so this is a longstanding
feature of antisemitism.

00:45:10.200 --> 00:45:12.150
When you look at this,

00:45:12.150 --> 00:45:15.210
Jews have been blamed or associated

00:45:15.210 --> 00:45:17.943
with the power of finance,
with the power of money.

00:45:20.094 --> 00:45:22.773
You see this also, I
mentioned in the talk,

00:45:23.760 --> 00:45:26.950
the way that this comes out

00:45:31.437 --> 00:45:32.783
in some anti-Zionist tropes,

00:45:34.019 --> 00:45:37.121
where again, this, the power
of money is emphasized,

00:45:37.121 --> 00:45:38.483
and I've provided some examples of that.

00:45:39.824 --> 00:45:41.661
And so this sort of parallels

00:45:41.661 --> 00:45:43.050
or corresponds to how these tropes

00:45:43.050 --> 00:45:47.673
have been used in
relationship to Jews directly.

00:45:49.950 --> 00:45:51.480
So I think it is a factor.

00:45:51.480 --> 00:45:53.607
I think it's a contributing factor.

00:45:53.607 --> 00:45:55.929
I think it's linked with the factors

00:45:55.929 --> 00:45:56.762
that I emphasized or that I focused

00:45:56.762 --> 00:45:59.593
on in complicated ways.

00:45:59.593 --> 00:46:03.480
But I do think it is
part of what's going on.

00:46:03.480 --> 00:46:06.300
The interesting question
to me is, you know,

00:46:06.300 --> 00:46:09.783
economic inequality has
been growing for decades,

00:46:10.620 --> 00:46:14.850
and yet antisemitism was on the decline

00:46:14.850 --> 00:46:16.413
until much more recently.

00:46:17.384 --> 00:46:18.420
And so if you would say, well,

00:46:18.420 --> 00:46:21.660
antisemitism is basically a response

00:46:21.660 --> 00:46:23.550
to growing economic inequality,

00:46:23.550 --> 00:46:25.050
what then explains the timing?

00:46:25.050 --> 00:46:29.820
Why is it so delayed
given that inequalities

00:46:29.820 --> 00:46:33.603
have been deepening for many years?

00:46:34.702 --> 00:46:36.780
So that's why I think by itself,

00:46:36.780 --> 00:46:39.093
this is not really a
sufficient explanation,

00:46:40.165 --> 00:46:43.470
but also, it seems to me
that it would have to be,

00:46:43.470 --> 00:46:45.570
it would have to be
taken into consideration

00:46:45.570 --> 00:46:49.173
for any kind of comprehensive
account of antisemitism today.

00:46:51.450 --> 00:46:53.037
- Great.

00:46:53.037 --> 00:46:54.810
This is a very good series of exchanges.

00:46:54.810 --> 00:46:56.763
Now I'm gonna speak,

00:46:58.609 --> 00:47:01.920
for Mari Samuel's question
after complimenting you

00:47:01.920 --> 00:47:04.050
for a great talk, quote.

00:47:04.050 --> 00:47:05.820
He asked this,

00:47:05.820 --> 00:47:08.365
my question is how you account

00:47:08.365 --> 00:47:12.060
for the fact that antisemitism
is rising globally,

00:47:12.060 --> 00:47:14.580
including in countries like France,

00:47:14.580 --> 00:47:17.100
which have not followed the same pattern

00:47:17.100 --> 00:47:19.473
of multiculturalism as in the US.

00:47:27.120 --> 00:47:27.953
- Interesting.

00:47:27.953 --> 00:47:28.786
Yeah.

00:47:30.660 --> 00:47:33.724
So the argument that I
develop here is specifically

00:47:33.724 --> 00:47:34.557
about the US,

00:47:38.078 --> 00:47:39.510
and I think that's a good question.

00:47:39.510 --> 00:47:41.190
I think we need more, you know,

00:47:41.190 --> 00:47:45.240
I am sort of a comparative as well

00:47:45.240 --> 00:47:47.296
as a historical sociologist.

00:47:47.296 --> 00:47:49.200
And so I think we need sort
of more comparative research

00:47:49.200 --> 00:47:52.200
because I a agree with
Mari that this is something

00:47:52.200 --> 00:47:54.783
that we see in many
countries around the world.

00:47:55.650 --> 00:48:00.650
And what it suggests to me is that, again,

00:48:00.720 --> 00:48:03.063
that there are multiple factors at work.

00:48:04.372 --> 00:48:06.847
I'm reminded here of
William Brustein's book

00:48:06.847 --> 00:48:08.037
"The Roots of Hate",

00:48:09.563 --> 00:48:11.970
which really try to get at these sort

00:48:11.970 --> 00:48:14.190
of multiple manifestations of antisemitism

00:48:14.190 --> 00:48:17.350
and the different forms that it took in

00:48:19.230 --> 00:48:21.745
the different sources of antisemitism

00:48:21.745 --> 00:48:23.733
that sometimes come together,

00:48:28.080 --> 00:48:30.363
I think in the European context.

00:48:33.090 --> 00:48:35.253
Yeah, I don't know how far I wanna go in.

00:48:35.253 --> 00:48:37.238
So I guess two things
I wanna say about this.

00:48:37.238 --> 00:48:38.106
Maybe I, you know,

00:48:38.106 --> 00:48:39.240
I hesitate to say too
much because I haven't,

00:48:39.240 --> 00:48:42.699
this is a question that I'm
not sure about the incident,

00:48:42.699 --> 00:48:44.552
and I think this requires more research,

00:48:44.552 --> 00:48:46.619
so I hesitate to say too much.

00:48:46.619 --> 00:48:48.137
But I wanna say two things.

00:48:48.137 --> 00:48:50.571
First of all, I forgot to mention this

00:48:50.571 --> 00:48:52.280
at the beginning of my talk.

00:48:52.280 --> 00:48:55.498
This paper I wanna say is part,

00:48:55.498 --> 00:48:56.394
I should have mentioned this before.

00:48:56.394 --> 00:48:57.600
It's part of a symposium
that's forthcoming

00:48:57.600 --> 00:49:00.210
in the American Journal
of Cultural Sociology.

00:49:00.210 --> 00:49:02.280
And those papers,

00:49:02.280 --> 00:49:04.920
I think provide some of
this comparative framing

00:49:04.920 --> 00:49:07.650
that you don't get in this paper alone.

00:49:07.650 --> 00:49:11.160
So my paper is focused
on the US in particular.

00:49:11.160 --> 00:49:12.840
There's another paper that Jeff

00:49:12.840 --> 00:49:15.480
and Tracy Adams contributed
to that symposium,

00:49:15.480 --> 00:49:17.670
which is really comparative in nature

00:49:17.670 --> 00:49:20.865
and tries to develop
a kind of theorization

00:49:20.865 --> 00:49:22.560
about comparative variations that we see

00:49:22.560 --> 00:49:24.960
in expressions of antisemitism.

00:49:24.960 --> 00:49:26.910
And I think does it really insightfully

00:49:26.910 --> 00:49:30.870
actually in a way that's both
historical and comparative.

00:49:30.870 --> 00:49:32.763
And then the third set in those,

00:49:36.186 --> 00:49:40.080
the third paper there deals
with the Scandinavian countries.

00:49:40.080 --> 00:49:41.250
So you, you get a kind of

00:49:41.250 --> 00:49:43.653
cross-national perspective
on antisemitism.

00:49:45.432 --> 00:49:47.100
And the other thing
that I was gonna say is

00:49:47.100 --> 00:49:51.660
I don't know how widespread this view is,

00:49:51.660 --> 00:49:54.750
but I am struck by the perspective

00:49:54.750 --> 00:49:57.123
of some European born intellectuals.

00:49:58.457 --> 00:50:00.570
I'm thinking of people like Alain Badiou

00:50:00.570 --> 00:50:04.560
Matty Bonzo and Enzo
Traverso who have insisted

00:50:04.560 --> 00:50:07.080
that Jews are now part of the core group,

00:50:07.080 --> 00:50:11.628
that after the Shah Jews
became privileged insiders

00:50:11.628 --> 00:50:14.280
in European societies in Western Europe,

00:50:14.280 --> 00:50:18.180
privileged insiders of a
dominant Judeo-Christian European

00:50:18.180 --> 00:50:21.540
or Western order at the
expense of new outgroups,

00:50:21.540 --> 00:50:22.743
particularly Muslims.

00:50:23.695 --> 00:50:25.895
I'm quite skeptical of
that argument myself,

00:50:27.410 --> 00:50:30.640
but I think that if I
were going to explore

00:50:32.272 --> 00:50:35.250
the roots of antisemitism in countries

00:50:35.250 --> 00:50:37.300
like France and other European countries,

00:50:38.188 --> 00:50:40.687
I would wanna make this
part of the analysis.

00:50:40.687 --> 00:50:42.480
I would wanna try to
understand to what extent

00:50:42.480 --> 00:50:43.870
this view is widely held

00:50:45.851 --> 00:50:48.690
and to what extent this view contributes

00:50:48.690 --> 00:50:50.290
to images of Jews as

00:50:53.633 --> 00:50:56.250
in the current political conjuncture,

00:50:56.250 --> 00:50:58.950
reactionary and anti-civil.

00:50:58.950 --> 00:51:00.150
So this would be something

00:51:00.150 --> 00:51:02.100
I would wanna explore further, I think.

00:51:03.854 --> 00:51:05.498
But I don't have a very good
answer to your question,

00:51:05.498 --> 00:51:07.433
Mari, because I haven't done
the comparative work myself.

00:51:09.510 --> 00:51:11.850
- Okay, now this is a question

00:51:11.850 --> 00:51:14.400
from that kind of relates

00:51:14.400 --> 00:51:17.133
to this discussion from Diane Louie.

00:51:18.750 --> 00:51:22.800
Does the anxiety regarding
boundary definition presuppose

00:51:22.800 --> 00:51:27.270
that the excluded group
retains inferiority

00:51:27.270 --> 00:51:29.283
in the mind of the core group?

00:51:30.270 --> 00:51:34.950
That is, is there a pervasive
stigma in the core group

00:51:34.950 --> 00:51:37.950
in being perceived as
having intersectionality

00:51:37.950 --> 00:51:39.453
with the excluded group?

00:51:42.360 --> 00:51:43.470
- Jeff, can you read that one more time?

00:51:43.470 --> 00:51:45.817
I'm not sure I fully
understood the question.

00:51:45.817 --> 00:51:48.900
- I don't understand the last sentence,

00:51:48.900 --> 00:51:51.390
but let me just repeat the first sentence

00:51:51.390 --> 00:51:54.843
'cause I do think you can address that.

00:51:55.930 --> 00:51:59.730
Does the anxiety regarding
boundary definitions presuppose

00:51:59.730 --> 00:52:03.490
that the excluded group
retains inferiority

00:52:04.676 --> 00:52:06.360
in the mind of the core group?

00:52:06.360 --> 00:52:07.290
In other words,

00:52:07.290 --> 00:52:10.320
I think they mean as it's
being incorporated speaks

00:52:10.320 --> 00:52:13.290
to what you had just talked about.

00:52:13.290 --> 00:52:14.253
- Yeah, yeah.

00:52:18.311 --> 00:52:19.144
I wouldn't put it that way.

00:52:19.144 --> 00:52:20.788
I wouldn't put it that way.

00:52:20.788 --> 00:52:23.650
You know, because I
think what is distinctive

00:52:24.565 --> 00:52:25.829
about the multicultural mode of

00:52:25.829 --> 00:52:29.343
incorporation as I
understand it, is that those,

00:52:30.617 --> 00:52:33.660
those outgroup qualities that
were perceived as stigmatizing

00:52:33.660 --> 00:52:38.660
the past become increasingly
destigmatized and even admired.

00:52:39.330 --> 00:52:42.483
I think what that does,

00:52:44.640 --> 00:52:47.470
it does fuel anxieties about

00:52:49.800 --> 00:52:54.000
identity and boundaries
and sort of definitions

00:52:54.000 --> 00:52:56.100
of sort of the core group.

00:52:56.100 --> 00:52:58.140
And among some core group members,

00:52:58.140 --> 00:53:01.650
I think that leads to an
effort to reassert hierarchical

00:53:01.650 --> 00:53:05.070
boundaries that multiculturalism
intends to dissolve.

00:53:05.070 --> 00:53:07.779
So I would put it a
little bit differently.

00:53:07.779 --> 00:53:11.823
I think this is not quite how
I would understand things.

00:53:15.517 --> 00:53:16.618
- Okay.

00:53:16.618 --> 00:53:18.367
I'm gonna now translate

00:53:18.367 --> 00:53:20.043
a question from Yada de Leon.

00:53:21.180 --> 00:53:24.720
Could you expand on how
other outgroup communities,

00:53:24.720 --> 00:53:26.310
other outgroup communities,

00:53:26.310 --> 00:53:29.160
especially black American communities,

00:53:29.160 --> 00:53:31.740
contribute to and or push back

00:53:31.740 --> 00:53:35.643
against this resurgence of antisemitism?

00:53:37.290 --> 00:53:39.540
I'm especially interested
in hearing more about

00:53:39.540 --> 00:53:42.060
the resentment aspect
that you'd mentioned.

00:53:42.060 --> 00:53:44.910
- Yeah, yeah.

00:53:44.910 --> 00:53:46.360
Also an interesting question.

00:53:48.030 --> 00:53:49.860
You know, again, here I
can be only tentative,

00:53:49.860 --> 00:53:51.746
you know, I haven't done,

00:53:51.746 --> 00:53:52.579
I haven't done the work, you know,

00:53:52.579 --> 00:53:54.868
the research that you know, would allow me

00:53:54.868 --> 00:53:57.270
to speak really
authoritatively about this.

00:53:57.270 --> 00:53:59.650
My sense, my impression is

00:54:02.460 --> 00:54:05.463
that within other outgroup communities,

00:54:06.930 --> 00:54:10.360
there is sometimes probably
a feeling of resentment

00:54:12.163 --> 00:54:14.993
to other outgroups that are
perceived to be more successful.

00:54:20.890 --> 00:54:22.380
But I think that I don't think

00:54:22.380 --> 00:54:24.905
that it would be fair to say that that

00:54:24.905 --> 00:54:28.590
sort of is the be all
and in all of attitudes

00:54:28.590 --> 00:54:30.570
in those other outgroup communities,

00:54:30.570 --> 00:54:33.090
there's also the possibility and sometimes

00:54:33.090 --> 00:54:38.090
the realization of solidarity
among those outgroups.

00:54:38.730 --> 00:54:39.690
Even when those act groups

00:54:39.690 --> 00:54:42.745
have sort of different relative degrees

00:54:42.745 --> 00:54:47.493
of sort of successful
multicultural incorporation.

00:54:49.080 --> 00:54:51.543
And I'm thinking in particular,

00:54:54.260 --> 00:54:55.110
I'm thinking in particular of an incident

00:54:55.110 --> 00:54:57.560
that happened on my own
campus several years ago.

00:54:59.781 --> 00:55:01.613
There was an anti-Semitic
incident on campus.

00:55:02.614 --> 00:55:03.930
There was a kind of,

00:55:03.930 --> 00:55:06.030
sort of a teaching that was held about it.

00:55:07.897 --> 00:55:09.480
And I remember the teaching

00:55:09.480 --> 00:55:12.180
was attended by lots of students.

00:55:12.180 --> 00:55:13.500
Some of them were Jewish,

00:55:13.500 --> 00:55:16.030
some of them were non-Jewish,

00:55:16.030 --> 00:55:17.423
and some of them were African-American.

00:55:20.636 --> 00:55:22.920
And initially the
discussion sort of started

00:55:22.920 --> 00:55:24.287
to fall into this groove
that you sometimes see

00:55:24.287 --> 00:55:29.059
in these kinds of
conversations about sort of

00:55:29.059 --> 00:55:31.350
who has suffered more historically.

00:55:31.350 --> 00:55:35.820
And I think these discussions
are always kind of pointless.

00:55:35.820 --> 00:55:38.320
I don't think they really
ever serve anybody well.

00:55:40.170 --> 00:55:42.931
Also, I dunno how you would sort

00:55:42.931 --> 00:55:44.581
of quantify degrees of suffering.

00:55:46.999 --> 00:55:49.549
And so it sort of went in
that direction initially.

00:55:50.803 --> 00:55:52.223
But by the end of the evening,

00:55:53.790 --> 00:55:58.770
I was struck that some of the same people

00:55:58.770 --> 00:56:00.900
who had sort of begun this way,

00:56:00.900 --> 00:56:03.060
had moved to a different way of talking

00:56:03.060 --> 00:56:06.450
and had begun to identify with each other

00:56:06.450 --> 00:56:08.213
in a way that they,

00:56:08.213 --> 00:56:10.050
I think maybe didn't at the
beginning of the evening

00:56:10.050 --> 00:56:13.110
and had begun to sort of identify

00:56:13.110 --> 00:56:15.811
some commonalities in their experiences.

00:56:15.811 --> 00:56:17.430
So their experiences were
by no means identical.

00:56:17.430 --> 00:56:19.233
I don't wanna suggest that they are,

00:56:21.188 --> 00:56:24.150
but they began to see some commonalities

00:56:24.150 --> 00:56:26.250
and they began to see each other not

00:56:26.250 --> 00:56:31.250
as sort of competitors
in terms of, you know,

00:56:31.470 --> 00:56:32.590
claiming the title of

00:56:33.588 --> 00:56:36.916
who has been most wronged historically,

00:56:36.916 --> 00:56:41.640
but as people who shared
not identical conditions,

00:56:41.640 --> 00:56:43.665
not identical situations,

00:56:43.665 --> 00:56:46.419
but situations with enough
elements shared in common

00:56:46.419 --> 00:56:48.900
that they could begin to perceive

00:56:48.900 --> 00:56:52.350
a way of working together
to move the campus

00:56:52.350 --> 00:56:54.900
in a more inclusive direction

00:56:54.900 --> 00:56:57.240
and to work together to do that.

00:56:57.240 --> 00:57:00.870
And I'd like to think
that it's still possible.

00:57:00.870 --> 00:57:03.750
I do think that it's
still possible though,

00:57:03.750 --> 00:57:05.799
I think for a variety of reasons

00:57:05.799 --> 00:57:09.090
there's many forces at work
in American society today

00:57:09.090 --> 00:57:11.523
that make that hard and difficult.

00:57:12.420 --> 00:57:13.980
But this too,

00:57:13.980 --> 00:57:16.200
I think remains a real possibility

00:57:16.200 --> 00:57:17.500
that is sometimes realized

00:57:18.411 --> 00:57:19.703
and practiced in American society.

00:57:21.390 --> 00:57:22.766
- Okay.

00:57:22.766 --> 00:57:24.630
Here are two more.

00:57:24.630 --> 00:57:26.770
I'd say specific questions

00:57:29.460 --> 00:57:31.233
from Laz Schneider.

00:57:32.117 --> 00:57:33.930
First, to what extent are anti-Semitic

00:57:33.930 --> 00:57:36.633
incidents related to Islamic issues,

00:57:37.889 --> 00:57:41.490
especially regarding in
relationship to Israel or otherwise?

00:57:41.490 --> 00:57:44.190
For example, Omar,

00:57:44.190 --> 00:57:49.190
to what can the increased black
anti-Semitism be attributed?

00:57:57.552 --> 00:57:58.719
- I mean, again, an interesting question.

00:57:58.719 --> 00:58:00.000
So my focus has been on the core group,

00:58:00.000 --> 00:58:02.015
on the American core group.

00:58:02.015 --> 00:58:02.848
And so this is really a question

00:58:02.848 --> 00:58:04.443
about groups outside of the core.

00:58:07.650 --> 00:58:09.422
This in a way,

00:58:09.422 --> 00:58:12.243
I think relates to Mari's
question about France.

00:58:13.286 --> 00:58:15.336
So, you know, so if the question is about

00:58:17.430 --> 00:58:21.393
antisemitism within Muslim
communities in the United States,

00:58:22.800 --> 00:58:24.903
I have no doubt that it exists.

00:58:25.770 --> 00:58:28.440
But I think this is a
much less of a problem

00:58:28.440 --> 00:58:31.800
in the United States than it
is in a place like France.

00:58:31.800 --> 00:58:34.380
Because Muslims as a percentage

00:58:34.380 --> 00:58:36.534
of the population in the United States,

00:58:36.534 --> 00:58:37.830
it's a much lower
percentage of the population

00:58:37.830 --> 00:58:39.810
in the US than it is in France.

00:58:39.810 --> 00:58:42.240
So I don't see Muslims as the sort

00:58:42.240 --> 00:58:47.240
of primary source of
antisemitism in this country.

00:58:49.380 --> 00:58:52.050
For one thing, there's not enough of them

00:58:52.050 --> 00:58:53.363
in order for them to play this role.

00:58:54.657 --> 00:58:58.383
And so this is what I would
say about the Islamic issues,

00:59:00.090 --> 00:59:02.430
you know, in terms of sort
of Muslims and blacks,

00:59:02.430 --> 00:59:05.250
you know, again, we're
talking about other outgroups,

00:59:05.250 --> 00:59:06.660
and here I, you know,

00:59:06.660 --> 00:59:11.660
I can simply repeat what I
said on the paper about this,

00:59:11.778 --> 00:59:15.168
that I think we have to distinguish

00:59:15.168 --> 00:59:17.580
the sources when antisemitism

00:59:17.580 --> 00:59:19.940
does arise within other outgroups,

00:59:19.940 --> 00:59:22.800
we have to distinguish
the factors at work,

00:59:22.800 --> 00:59:24.960
the dynamics there from the core group,

00:59:24.960 --> 00:59:27.390
because I think the
dynamics are different.

00:59:27.390 --> 00:59:30.220
And I think sometimes

00:59:31.710 --> 00:59:33.900
there is a kind of politics of resentment

00:59:33.900 --> 00:59:35.013
that is at work here.

00:59:36.030 --> 00:59:39.580
But I also think that

00:59:41.460 --> 00:59:45.510
an analysis of the degree
to which antisemitism exists

00:59:45.510 --> 00:59:47.250
in these communities also has

00:59:47.250 --> 00:59:52.250
to take into consideration
the way in which

00:59:52.590 --> 00:59:54.630
the multicultural incorporation

00:59:54.630 --> 00:59:58.320
of these groups has been less successful.

00:59:58.320 --> 01:00:02.610
And this is, yeah,

01:00:02.610 --> 01:00:04.343
well, I'll just leave it there for now.

01:00:05.850 --> 01:00:06.683
- Thank you.

01:00:08.160 --> 01:00:10.590
Here is another specific question.

01:00:10.590 --> 01:00:12.573
I think we're beginning to wrap up.

01:00:14.040 --> 01:00:16.674
What is this,

01:00:16.674 --> 01:00:18.330
what is the relationship
between anti-Semitism

01:00:18.330 --> 01:00:20.433
and anti-Israel sentiments,

01:00:21.781 --> 01:00:24.531
I.e. the critical view of what the state

01:00:24.531 --> 01:00:25.943
of Israel has been doing to Arabs?

01:00:26.886 --> 01:00:28.890
To me, it seems paradoxical

01:00:28.890 --> 01:00:30.750
that alt-right figures like Trump

01:00:30.750 --> 01:00:33.640
are somehow supportive
of the Israeli government

01:00:34.925 --> 01:00:38.010
while instigating anti-Semitic
sentiments themselves.

01:00:38.010 --> 01:00:39.720
- Yeah, yeah.

01:00:39.720 --> 01:00:40.553
Another great question.

01:00:40.553 --> 01:00:45.090
I, you know, I would make a distinction.

01:00:45.090 --> 01:00:46.620
I would want to make a distinction

01:00:46.620 --> 01:00:49.653
between criticism of Israel.

01:00:51.030 --> 01:00:56.030
And right now, I think, and I'm speaking,

01:00:56.070 --> 01:00:58.590
you know, just personally
not as a, you know,

01:00:58.590 --> 01:01:03.390
this is not a sociological statement.

01:01:03.390 --> 01:01:04.650
This is a personal statement right now.

01:01:04.650 --> 01:01:07.140
I think there's a lot to criticize

01:01:07.140 --> 01:01:08.973
in the current government in Israel.

01:01:10.170 --> 01:01:13.593
I would distinguish
that from anti-Zionism,

01:01:14.460 --> 01:01:17.433
and anti-Zionism I would
think of as a kind of,

01:01:18.300 --> 01:01:22.120
as yet another kind of
political ideology in which

01:01:26.525 --> 01:01:29.340
the existence of a Jewish
national homeland in Palestine

01:01:29.340 --> 01:01:30.990
is considered illegitimate,

01:01:30.990 --> 01:01:31.860
that it was illegitimate

01:01:31.860 --> 01:01:34.290
from the beginning, remains illegitimate.

01:01:34.290 --> 01:01:37.260
And so this is a different,

01:01:37.260 --> 01:01:39.513
I think different kind of thing.

01:01:42.510 --> 01:01:45.240
I am certainly not somebody who thinks

01:01:45.240 --> 01:01:47.820
that criticism of Israel is inherently,

01:01:47.820 --> 01:01:50.313
or by definition, anti-Semitic.

01:01:53.520 --> 01:01:55.570
I don't even think that anti-Zionism

01:01:56.460 --> 01:01:58.696
is inherently anti-Semitic,

01:01:58.696 --> 01:02:00.184
although I think there's a lot of overlap

01:02:00.184 --> 01:02:02.463
between anti-Zionism
and anti-Semitism today.

01:02:03.816 --> 01:02:05.700
And the way that I tend to
think about this is a way

01:02:05.700 --> 01:02:09.630
that here I'm influenced
by Mitchell Cohen,

01:02:09.630 --> 01:02:12.450
who wrote a piece in
2003 along these lines,

01:02:12.450 --> 01:02:14.716
who talked about the ways that

01:02:14.716 --> 01:02:17.520
anti-Zionist discourses ways of talking,

01:02:17.520 --> 01:02:19.020
ways of thinking,

01:02:19.020 --> 01:02:20.650
position Zionist or Israel

01:02:21.570 --> 01:02:25.263
in ways analogous to how
antisemitism positions Jews.

01:02:26.457 --> 01:02:28.860
And that I actually think
Cohen was onto something.

01:02:28.860 --> 01:02:31.010
I think there's a lot
of evidence for that.

01:02:33.558 --> 01:02:36.358
And that's what I tried to
suggest in the paper as well.

01:02:38.010 --> 01:02:40.860
- Okay, I'm gonna ask you
really two more questions,

01:02:40.860 --> 01:02:42.813
and then we'll call it a day.

01:02:44.760 --> 01:02:46.050
By David Silverberg.

01:02:46.050 --> 01:02:48.595
It's a pretty long question,

01:02:48.595 --> 01:02:50.258
but I think it's an interesting one.

01:02:50.258 --> 01:02:53.810
He says he's piggybacking
off a previous answer

01:02:53.810 --> 01:02:56.360
about Jewish incorporation
into the dominant group,

01:02:58.789 --> 01:03:00.600
Alain Badiou, et cetera.

01:03:00.600 --> 01:03:02.472
He says, I have a question

01:03:02.472 --> 01:03:04.890
about where the reassertion of whiteness

01:03:04.890 --> 01:03:08.575
as the primary defining sociological frame

01:03:08.575 --> 01:03:11.130
in the United States fits in.

01:03:11.130 --> 01:03:14.610
This seems important because one,

01:03:14.610 --> 01:03:17.880
whiteness in the US is obviously unstable.

01:03:17.880 --> 01:03:19.860
There's a ton of work on the incorporation

01:03:19.860 --> 01:03:22.110
of different ethnic
groups across disciplines.

01:03:22.110 --> 01:03:25.260
And two, because Unite
the Right event raised

01:03:25.260 --> 01:03:27.960
in this presentation clearly is hostile,

01:03:27.960 --> 01:03:29.583
not just towards Jews,

01:03:31.265 --> 01:03:36.003
but to many other groups
based on whiteness.

01:03:38.070 --> 01:03:40.800
So how are you factoring or not factoring

01:03:40.800 --> 01:03:43.710
in whiteness as an in-group identity?

01:03:43.710 --> 01:03:46.260
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:03:46.260 --> 01:03:48.860
I have sort of bracketed
the question in this paper.

01:03:52.386 --> 01:03:53.970
So, you know, and I
think really addressing

01:03:55.376 --> 01:03:58.500
this in the detail and
depth that it needs to be,

01:03:58.500 --> 01:04:00.150
would require a paper of its own.

01:04:01.232 --> 01:04:02.603
And there's a lot being
written about this.

01:04:04.110 --> 01:04:06.060
I agree with the points

01:04:06.060 --> 01:04:09.810
about whiteness being something unstable.

01:04:09.810 --> 01:04:11.640
The boundaries of whiteness have, we know,

01:04:11.640 --> 01:04:14.913
have been contested and
shifted over time historically,

01:04:19.418 --> 01:04:20.251
there is,

01:04:23.256 --> 01:04:24.813
so we know that.

01:04:25.711 --> 01:04:29.280
I would also say that whiteness
is another one of these sort

01:04:29.280 --> 01:04:31.030
of primordial qualities by which

01:04:31.930 --> 01:04:34.133
the American core group has
historically been defined.

01:04:35.978 --> 01:04:37.710
And the relationship of Jews to whiteness

01:04:38.556 --> 01:04:40.950
is sort of interesting one,

01:04:40.950 --> 01:04:42.240
Eric Goldstein and others have written

01:04:42.240 --> 01:04:45.003
about this very perceptively.

01:04:46.050 --> 01:04:47.970
I think this would have to be part

01:04:47.970 --> 01:04:49.570
of a wider conversation

01:04:52.350 --> 01:04:54.300
about core group and its relationship

01:04:54.300 --> 01:04:56.073
to outgroups in American history.

01:04:58.232 --> 01:05:01.270
But maybe the last thing
I'll say about this is that

01:05:03.360 --> 01:05:06.100
one of the things that
sometimes bothers me

01:05:07.145 --> 01:05:08.474
about these sort of discussions

01:05:08.474 --> 01:05:10.083
about Jews and whiteness is,

01:05:12.472 --> 01:05:14.850
I have a feeling sometimes
that these discussions become,

01:05:14.850 --> 01:05:16.986
they start to revolve around

01:05:16.986 --> 01:05:17.843
the question of whether Jews are white,

01:05:19.013 --> 01:05:20.430
whether Jews have ever been white,

01:05:20.430 --> 01:05:22.800
when did they become white,
are they still white?

01:05:22.800 --> 01:05:25.293
Who has the authority
to define Jews racially?

01:05:27.688 --> 01:05:29.488
And those are interesting questions,

01:05:30.750 --> 01:05:31.650
but what I worry about,

01:05:31.650 --> 01:05:32.703
I guess, is that,

01:05:35.670 --> 01:05:36.753
in a way,

01:05:42.696 --> 01:05:43.620
I have a feeling that
these discussions sometimes

01:05:43.620 --> 01:05:45.570
in a kind of Procrustean fashion,

01:05:45.570 --> 01:05:48.573
try to squeeze Jews into other categories.

01:05:50.345 --> 01:05:51.930
And I'm always struck by the fact

01:05:51.930 --> 01:05:54.990
that antisemitism is something

01:05:54.990 --> 01:05:58.143
that Jews can suffer from
and be victimized by,

01:06:00.190 --> 01:06:01.530
regardless of their
racial status of whether

01:06:01.530 --> 01:06:05.430
they're sort of perceived and
defined as as white or not.

01:06:05.430 --> 01:06:07.080
And I think this sometimes

01:06:07.080 --> 01:06:09.210
gets lost in these discussions.

01:06:09.210 --> 01:06:14.043
It sort of falls by the wayside
when the discussion comes,

01:06:15.120 --> 01:06:20.120
starts to be focused exclusively on color.

01:06:23.546 --> 01:06:24.900
And well, if we had more time, you know,

01:06:24.900 --> 01:06:27.840
I would invoke some things
that Dubois wrote late

01:06:27.840 --> 01:06:29.540
in his life and late in his career

01:06:30.535 --> 01:06:33.285
about the Jewish question
where he sort of acknowledged

01:06:34.157 --> 01:06:36.870
that early in his career
he tended to think of race,

01:06:36.870 --> 01:06:40.863
racism, racial conflict
exclusively in terms of color.

01:06:42.075 --> 01:06:45.019
And later came to see that
it was a more multifaceted

01:06:45.019 --> 01:06:47.490
and more complicated kind
of social phenomenon.

01:06:47.490 --> 01:06:51.003
And I tend to agree with
Dubois on on this point.

01:06:51.840 --> 01:06:54.480
I think those kinds of things
get, sometimes get lost,

01:06:54.480 --> 01:06:56.700
not necessarily, but sometimes get lost

01:06:56.700 --> 01:07:00.090
when the conversation shifts to questions

01:07:00.090 --> 01:07:02.940
about whiteness in the
relationship of Jews to whiteness.

01:07:04.343 --> 01:07:05.910
- Thanks.

01:07:05.910 --> 01:07:10.143
I'm gonna ask you the last
question then add on something

01:07:11.400 --> 01:07:14.430
from me which relates to that.

01:07:14.430 --> 01:07:17.675
Michael Alnik asks,

01:07:17.675 --> 01:07:21.810
do trends in anti-Semitic
incidents and hate crimes

01:07:21.810 --> 01:07:26.560
necessarily index trends in anti-Semitism

01:07:28.380 --> 01:07:31.170
among the general American population?

01:07:31.170 --> 01:07:33.780
And I think that's a good question,

01:07:33.780 --> 01:07:36.610
and I was thinking that

01:07:38.130 --> 01:07:42.660
whether the indexing,

01:07:42.660 --> 01:07:45.690
you saw the disturbing index
and we're all aware of it,

01:07:45.690 --> 01:07:48.963
of anti-Semitic incidents and hate crimes,

01:07:50.760 --> 01:07:53.040
and I think you know this

01:07:53.040 --> 01:07:55.770
from my own paper in our symposium,

01:07:55.770 --> 01:08:00.770
but does this indicate an
increase in anti-Semitic beliefs

01:08:01.770 --> 01:08:06.770
or an increase in public
anti-Semitic actions?

01:08:08.699 --> 01:08:12.063
In other words, a kind of disinhibition,

01:08:13.770 --> 01:08:17.670
which doesn't mean that
there's an increase

01:08:17.670 --> 01:08:19.800
of anti-Semitic beliefs.

01:08:19.800 --> 01:08:21.633
I don't want to, you know,

01:08:22.800 --> 01:08:24.180
black out the first question.

01:08:24.180 --> 01:08:27.270
I think they're related to each other.

01:08:27.270 --> 01:08:29.490
- Yeah, yeah.

01:08:29.490 --> 01:08:31.380
Well first I'll just say hello to Michael.

01:08:31.380 --> 01:08:33.537
Michael is a friend and colleague,

01:08:33.537 --> 01:08:36.087
so it's great that you're
able to be here, Michael.

01:08:37.948 --> 01:08:41.973
So I focused on incidents
for a couple of reasons.

01:08:43.560 --> 01:08:46.770
You know, data on incidents
are readily available.

01:08:46.770 --> 01:08:47.850
They're sort of organizations

01:08:47.850 --> 01:08:49.350
that are collecting this data,

01:08:52.997 --> 01:08:54.523
and number one, number two,

01:09:00.815 --> 01:09:02.860
I'm enough of a pragmatist to think that

01:09:06.948 --> 01:09:10.530
beliefs that don't have
practical consequences

01:09:10.530 --> 01:09:14.310
are perhaps less interesting.

01:09:14.310 --> 01:09:15.933
And so,

01:09:20.160 --> 01:09:22.910
and I think that's a sort of

01:09:22.910 --> 01:09:26.100
a view that many people would hold.

01:09:26.100 --> 01:09:28.900
So of course we're concerned
about anti-Semitic beliefs,

01:09:30.573 --> 01:09:32.640
but we're most concerned
about those beliefs

01:09:32.640 --> 01:09:35.760
when they find expression
in anti-Semitic action

01:09:35.760 --> 01:09:37.563
or anti-Semitic practices.

01:09:41.040 --> 01:09:43.810
The question of whether these incidents

01:09:46.260 --> 01:09:50.770
indicates a growth in beliefs or simply

01:09:52.615 --> 01:09:54.270
a weakening of the prohibitions against

01:09:54.270 --> 01:09:55.860
acting on those beliefs or expressing

01:09:55.860 --> 01:09:58.650
those beliefs is an interesting one.

01:09:58.650 --> 01:10:00.660
I don't know the answer to that question.

01:10:00.660 --> 01:10:03.930
And I think the data that I have here,

01:10:03.930 --> 01:10:05.520
that I used in this paper
and that I presented

01:10:05.520 --> 01:10:08.797
this paper doesn't allow
us to answer that question.

01:10:08.797 --> 01:10:13.797
I think the ADL and some
other Jewish groups are trying

01:10:13.950 --> 01:10:16.590
to get at the beliefs question

01:10:16.590 --> 01:10:18.783
more directly with survey data.

01:10:22.975 --> 01:10:25.070
And the problem with that is if

01:10:27.210 --> 01:10:30.480
you wanna see how these beliefs
sort of change over time,

01:10:30.480 --> 01:10:32.730
you need a kind of
longitudinal study, right?

01:10:34.259 --> 01:10:35.220
So it's not enough to have a snapshot

01:10:36.563 --> 01:10:39.019
of what the beliefs are this year.

01:10:39.019 --> 01:10:39.852
It doesn't tell us much if we don't

01:10:39.852 --> 01:10:40.685
know what the beliefs were,

01:10:40.685 --> 01:10:41.880
what they looked like five years ago

01:10:41.880 --> 01:10:44.613
or 10 years ago or 25 years ago.

01:10:45.688 --> 01:10:46.521
And I'm not sure there's really

01:10:46.521 --> 01:10:48.030
good longitudinal data about that.

01:10:48.030 --> 01:10:49.532
Maybe there is.

01:10:49.532 --> 01:10:51.093
I'm not sure that there is,

01:10:51.930 --> 01:10:54.180
so I think it's an important question.

01:10:54.180 --> 01:10:56.460
It's a question that I'll say that

01:10:56.460 --> 01:10:58.410
I don't know the answer to,

01:10:58.410 --> 01:11:01.863
and I think it requires more research.

01:11:04.590 --> 01:11:09.590
- Chad, I wanna thank you for
this very stimulating paper

01:11:10.410 --> 01:11:14.790
about a subject that is
immensely depressing,

01:11:14.790 --> 01:11:18.450
but your talk was not depressing,

01:11:18.450 --> 01:11:22.230
but inspiring and your
open-minded response

01:11:22.230 --> 01:11:25.530
to the questions has been just great.

01:11:25.530 --> 01:11:28.410
So thank you very much on behalf

01:11:28.410 --> 01:11:31.170
of this community and we look forward.

01:11:31.170 --> 01:11:33.720
- Thank you, Jeff.
- Your work in the future.

01:11:33.720 --> 01:11:35.280
- Thanks so much.

01:11:35.280 --> 01:11:36.240
- Okay.

01:11:36.240 --> 01:11:37.323
Bye, everybody.

